    ("SELF_WAKE_ENABLED", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (**ON under POLYROB_LOCAL + AUTONOMY_ENABLED**)", "W1: re-enter an idle session as a forged continuation turn.", "advanced"),
    ("SELF_WAKE_MAX_REENTRIES", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`3`", "Per-session self-wake depth cap.", "advanced"),
    ("SELF_WAKE_IDLE_BACKOFF_SEC", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`30`", "Idle backoff before a self-wake re-entry.", "advanced"),
    ("BACKGROUND_REVIEW_ENABLED", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (**ON under POLYROB_LOCAL + AUTONOMY_ENABLED**)", "W2: fork a cheap aux reviewer every N productive turns.", "advanced"),
    ("BG_REVIEW_INTERVAL", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`10`", "Productive-turn interval between background reviews.", "advanced"),
    ("BG_REVIEW_MAX_STEPS", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`8`", "Max steps for a background-review fork.", "advanced"),
    ("CRON_RUN_LOOP", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "**ON**", "cron jobs actually run `run_session` (not just create an idle session).", "advanced"),
    ("CRON_DELIVERY_ENABLED", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF", "Deliver cron results out-of-band (telegram/email/twitter).", "advanced"),
    ("CRON_WRITE_JOBS_ENABLED", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF", "A cron job carrying `payload.write_verb` runs ONE allowlisted WRITE verb with no session and no model turn — today only `agent_nft.agent_nft_collection_reveal` (the collection revealer: `reveal(ids)` on a pinned collection, gas only). OFF: every such tick is a $0 `cron_run skipp…", "advanced"),
    ("OWNER_DIGEST_ENABLED", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF", "Owner daily digest: a cron job carrying `payload.digest` is composed deterministically ($0, no model turn) from the unified ledger + event log + open asks and pushed via the delivery rail. Requires `CRON_DELIVERY_ENABLED` for the actual send. Create the job with `polyrob cron sc…", "advanced"),
    ("CRON_DELIVERY_ALLOW_EXPLICIT_TARGET", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF", "Allow an explicit (non-tenant-default) delivery target.", "advanced"),
    ("SEND_MESSAGE_USER_DELIVERY", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "**ON**", "§3.1 communication contract: the agent's `send_message` in an AUTONOMOUS session (goal/cron/planner) routes to the session's OWN principal through the one user-delivery rail instead of dying in the session feed (the lost-blocker-report class). Strict scope: own principal only —…", "advanced"),
    ("USER_DELIVERY_DEDUP_HOURS", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`24`", "§3.2 rail memory: identical content (per tenant, content-hash) that the owner ACTUALLY RECEIVED within this window is suppressed (`deduped`). ⚠️ 2026-09-15: it keys on delivered content only — matching an `undelivered` fallback made a failed send permanent (the retry came back `…", "advanced"),
    ("USER_DELIVERY_RATE_PER_HOUR", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`10`", "§3.2 rail memory: max user-bound sends per tenant per rolling hour (agent sends + cron delivery + framework notices share the budget; the CRITICAL lane is exempt and does not consume it). Pref `delivery.rate_per_hour` WINS unless this variable is explicitly set, in which case it…", "advanced"),
    ("USER_DELIVERY_DAILY_CAP", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`30`", "§3.2 rail memory: max user-bound sends per tenant per rolling 24h. ⚠️ 2026-09-15: the CRITICAL lane (approvals, blocked goals, executed transactions, credit/security notices) is exempt AND no longer consumes the window — on prod those lanes had been spending the whole budget tha…", "public"),
    ("USER_DELIVERY_RESERVED_SLOTS", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`8`", "Slots of `USER_DELIVERY_DAILY_CAP` that `priority=\"low\"` traffic (e.g. goal-start pings) may NOT consume, so goal completions + the daily digest keep headroom. Clamped to leave ≥1 slot for low traffic. Safety-bearing sources (`credit_sentinel`/`halt`/`security`) bypass the cap a…", "advanced"),
    ("CHAT_PATH_LINKS", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "**ON**", "A filesystem path is not an address (communication contract C4). A workspace path in an agent-authored message is resolved to something the reader can open — attached when the surface carries media and the file passes the attach screen, else a console URL (`WEBVIEW_PUBLIC_URL`),…", "advanced"),
    ("USER_DELIVERY_SPILL", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "**ON**", "Long-body spill (chat-first review 2026-08-22, G8): an owner-bound body over `USER_DELIVERY_SPILL_CHARS` is written to a report file under `<data_home>/outbox/`, attached, and replaced by a short gist. ONE rail policy, so every producer (goal completions, cron delivery, escalati…", "advanced"),
    ("USER_DELIVERY_SPILL_CHARS", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`1200`", "Body length above which the rail spills to an attachment. Deliberately well under one Telegram message (4096) — the goal is a body the owner reads at a glance, not one that merely avoids chunking.", "advanced"),
    ("USER_DELIVERY_GIST_CHARS", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`600`", "Character budget for the gist that replaces a spilled body. Whole leading lines only (never a mid-sentence cut), plus any `Console:`/link line lifted from the tail so truncation cannot drop the actionable part.", "advanced"),
    ("TELEMETRY_EVENT_LOG_PATH", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "unset", "Override the durable telemetry event log's db path (default: `<data_root>/telemetry_events.db`). The test suite uses this to keep telemetry (and the §3.2 delivery-rail memory) out of the real data home.", "advanced"),
    ("TOKEN_DENYLIST_PATH", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "unset", "Override the 043 W5 owner-session token denylist db path (default: `<data_root>/token_denylist.db`). Holds the `jti`s that `/logout` revokes; the auth gates refuse a token whose jti is listed. Mainly a test seam so revocations stay out of the real data home.", "internal"),
    ("RUN_EVENTS_ENABLED", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "**ON**", "master gate for the span/wait feed events (`tool_started` / `llm_started` / `awaiting_approval` / `approval_resolved`, plus the P1 compaction/retry/sub-agent/delegation kinds) that let every surface show what the agent is doing RIGHT NOW (in-flight tool, thinking, blocked approv…", "internal"),
    ("TELEGRAM_PROGRESS_EDITS", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "**ON**", "the Telegram `⚙️ Working…` bubble becomes a live status line (throttled in-place edits ≤1/2.5s: current tool / step / tool count / elapsed / cost, wait states override immediately — `⏸ Waiting for your approval`, `↻ retrying`, `📦 compacting`). Per-owner opt-out via pref `progres…", "advanced"),
    ("AUTONOMY_START_NOTICE", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "**OFF in every posture**", "One-line owner notice when an autonomous goal/cron run STARTS (`▶ goal started: …`) via the one delivery rail (dedup + caps), `priority=\"low\"` on both legs. Digest/$0-gated ticks never notify. OFF in every posture, including `AUTONOMY_POSTURE=full`: a start is already visible on…", "advanced"),
    ("TICKER_IDLE_BACKOFF_ENABLED", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (**ON under POLYROB_LOCAL**)", "Cron + goal-dispatch background tickers back off their poll interval on idle ticks (nothing due) instead of firing at a fixed cadence forever — cuts CPU wakeups/battery drain on a single-user local CLI.", "advanced"),
    ("TICKER_IDLE_BACKOFF_MAX_MULTIPLIER", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`5`", "Cap on how many multiples of a ticker's base interval idle backoff may reach (e.g. 5x a 60s base = 300s worst-case staleness).", "advanced"),
    ("GOALS_ENABLED", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (**ON under POLYROB_LOCAL + AUTONOMY_ENABLED**)", "W4: durable cross-session goal board + dispatcher.", "public"),
    ("GOAL_MAX_RETRIES", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`2`", "Goal circuit-breaker failure threshold.", "advanced"),
    ("GOAL_CLAIM_TTL_SEC", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`900`", "Goal claim lease TTL.", "advanced"),
    ("GOAL_YIELD_FOR_MONEY_RAIL", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (`false`)", "056 WS5 (D1, owner-approved 2026-09-19): a cron job that may PRE-EMPT (`payload.preempts`, which defaults to `payload.priority == \"money\"`; `polyrob cron edit <id> --preempts/--no-preempts`) that comes due while a BOARD GOAL holds the shared workspace pre-empts it — the goal's r…", "advanced"),
    ("GOAL_DEFAULT_MAX_STEPS", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`30`", "056 WS5: the step budget for a goal whose payload sets none (was a literal 20). `goal_create` now exposes `max_steps` (6–60).", "advanced"),
    ("GOAL_DISPATCH_CRON_HEADROOM_SEC", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`0` (off)", "Defer starting a board goal while an enabled cron job is due within this many seconds (overdue and currently RUNNING included). On a shared project-root workspace a goal run marks the process busy and cron ticks skip until it ends, so a goal started minutes before a due money ra…", "advanced"),
    ("GOAL_MAX_RUN_SECONDS", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`1800`", "Hard wall-clock cap on a single goal run (mirrors cron); a timeout is recorded as a failure and the slot is reclaimed.", "advanced"),
    ("GOAL_DISPATCH_INTERVAL_SEC", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`60`", "Goal dispatcher tick interval.", "advanced"),
    ("GOAL_MAX_CONCURRENT", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`2`", "Max concurrent goal runs.", "public"),
    ("GOAL_FAIR_DISPATCH", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "**ON**", "Round-robin the ready queue across objectives instead of the global `priority DESC, created_at` order, so one objective's backlog cannot take every dispatch slot while its neighbours starve. Priority still decides who is served FIRST within a pass; throughput is unchanged when o…", "internal"),
    ("GOAL_PER_OBJECTIVE_CAP", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`0` (disabled)", "OPTIONAL hard ceiling on concurrent goal runs belonging to ONE objective, on top of the round-robin. `0` (default) means no per-objective ceiling — the round-robin alone spreads the slots and never idles one. Set `1` to guarantee a stream can never hold two slots even when nothi…", "advanced"),
    ("GOAL_PLANNER_ENABLED", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (**ON under POLYROB_LOCAL + AUTONOMY_ENABLED**)", "Goal-planner feature gate.", "advanced"),
    ("GOAL_PLANNER_MIN_READY", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`2`", "Min ready goals before planner triggers.", "advanced"),
    ("GOAL_PLANNER_COOLDOWN_SEC", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`3600`", "Planner cooldown (seconds).", "advanced"),
    ("GOAL_PLANNER_HISTORY_N", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`10`", "Planner goal history window.", "advanced"),
    ("GOAL_PLANNER_SCALING", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "**ON**", "ONE revert for the whole planner half of stream scaling (`GOAL_FAIR_DISPATCH` reverts the dispatch half). `=false` restores the pre-scaling planner byte-for-byte: the derived ready ceiling falls back to the fixed `PLANNER_READY_FLOOR` (5, the old \"Never exceed 5 ready goals tota…", "internal"),
    ("GOAL_PLANNER_GOALS_PER_RUN", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`3`", "Upper bound on goals ONE planner run may create (\"Create 1-N goals\" in the planner prompt). Deliberately does NOT scale with the objective count — raising it raises spend per run, not coverage; coverage comes from the starvation order and the ready ceiling.", "advanced"),
    ("GOAL_PLANNER_READY_CEILING", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`0` (derive)", "Ready-goal ceiling the planner is told to respect, and the thinness gate `_maybe_plan` uses. `0` derives it as `max(5, active_objective_count)`, so a 16-stream board is allowed 16 ready goals instead of the legacy hardcoded 5 — five ready goals cannot cover sixteen streams. Any…", "advanced"),
    ("GOAL_PLANNER_MAX_SOCIAL", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`1`", "How many goals in one planner run may carry the `twitter` tool. Was the hardcoded \"At most ONE goal may include 'twitter'\". Raise it only with the outbound send cap in mind — it multiplies posting volume, not coverage.", "advanced"),
    ("GOAL_DAILY_QUOTA", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`6`", "Max goal runs started per trailing 24h; <=0 disables.", "public"),
    ("GOAL_SELF_WAKE_ENABLED", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (**ON under `AUTONOMY_POSTURE` owner-visible/full**)", "Goal-initiated self-wake re-entry — gates whether the dispatcher *attempts* delivery (`agents/task/goals/dispatcher.py::_self_wake`). Required combination: this alone is not sufficient — the delivery producer (`TaskAgent.deliver_self_wake`) separately no-ops unless `SELF_WAKE_EN…", "advanced"),
    ("GOAL_NOTIFY_ON_DONE", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "ON", "§3.4 SAFETY NET (demoted from unconditional push): tell the user when a background goal completes only when the agent itself said nothing during the run (`RunOutcome.user_messages` empty) — the agent's own `send_message` (delivered live via the §3.1 rail) is the primary channel.…", "advanced"),
    ("GOAL_DEDUP_THRESHOLD", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`0.6`", "Goal dedup similarity threshold (0.0–1.0).", "advanced"),
    ("AUTONOMY_HALT", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF", "Legacy facet of the 031 owner pause record — read, never written. The ONE runtime pause state is `<data_dir>/AUTONOMY_PAUSE.json` (scopes `all`/`trading`/`streams`/`planner`/`cron`/`social`/`oversight`/`pings`, optional expiry, atomic, fail-closed: an unreadable record is a paus…", "public"),
    ("TREASURY_ENTRY_PAUSE", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF", "Legacy facet of the owner pause record — the `trading` scope: refuse NEW treasury positions (any chain, any turn origin) while still allowing exits (sells to the chain's quote asset, revokes). Set it live with `polyrob autonomy pause trading` / `polyrob owner pause-entries` / `/…", "advanced"),
    ("STREAM_SEEDING_PAUSE", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF", "Legacy facet of the owner pause record — the `streams` scope: refuse NEW seeds from an operator's stream manifest (the file `POLYROB_STREAMS_MANIFEST` names, else `<data_home>/streams/streams.yaml`) while live goals, ad-hoc goals and cron run on. Set it live with `polyrob autono…", "advanced"),
    ("CURATOR_ENABLED", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (**ON under POLYROB_LOCAL + AUTONOMY_ENABLED**)", "stale/archive unused authored skills (Phase 1, no LLM).", "advanced"),
    ("CURATOR_INTERVAL_HOURS", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`168`", "Curator tick interval (hours).", "advanced"),
    ("CURATOR_STALE_DAYS", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`30`", "Days unused before a skill is staled.", "advanced"),
    ("CURATOR_ARCHIVE_DAYS", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`90`", "Days before stale skill is archived.", "advanced"),
    ("SANDBOX_REAP_ENABLED", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "**ON**", "043 A8/A42: the ownership-keyed sandbox-container sweep (removes a persistent docker sandbox whose owning session is gone; hourly-ish, `_SANDBOX_REAP_INTERVAL_SEC`=900s) — distinct from the AGE-based cold-start `reap_orphans`, which never runs periodically. No-op unless persiste…", "advanced"),
    ("INSIGHTS_TOOL", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (**ON under POLYROB_LOCAL + AUTONOMY_ENABLED**)", "W7: read-only authored-skill reuse-% `insights` action.", "advanced"),
    ("AGENT_STATUS_TOOL", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (**ON under POLYROB_LOCAL**)", "I-6: read-only `agent_status` introspection action — steps used/remaining, active tools, context-token usage, wallet + tenant ledger; every section fails soft independently.", "advanced"),
    ("AVATAR_TOOL_ENABLED", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (**ON under POLYROB_LOCAL**)", "The `agent_avatar` action: the agent reads its avatar slot (set / not set / unreadable, and the source), `attach=true` copies the image into the session workspace so `message(media_paths=[...])` can deliver it, and `set_from` (a workspace image, a URL, or `nft:chain:contract:id`…", "advanced"),
    ("LIVE_HEALTH_CONTEXT", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`true`", "2026-08-28 status SSOT: at the first step of every turn the agent receives a `<live-health>` control note rendered from the SAME `core/status_snapshot.py` snapshot the owner's `/status` shows (credit sentinel, live provider, open asks, blocked goals, suppressed owner notices, de…", "advanced"),
    ("VERIFY_BEFORE_DONE", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (**ON under POLYROB_LOCAL**)", "I-3 / H3 (dedup decision D1): when the run's action ledger shows a successful code edit (`str_replace`/`apply_patch`/`create_file`/`move_file`/`delete_file`) more recent than the last successful `run_tests` (or with no `run_tests` at all), the first `done()` is intercepted with…", "advanced"),
    ("PROJECT_CONTEXT_AUTOLOAD", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (**ON under POLYROB_LOCAL**)", "C9: auto-load a project file as a frozen `PROJECT_CONTEXT` foundation message. Names by precedence: `polyrob.md` > `POLYROB.md` > `AGENTS.md` > `CLAUDE.md` > `.cursorrules` (highest-precedence name that exists wins; not concatenated). Local = trusted/steering.", "advanced"),
    ("ENV_CONTEXT_BLOCK", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "ON", "014-C1: pin the `<environment>` foundation block (instance, platform, data dir, absolute workspace path + persistence semantics, posture axes, host-executable probe) so the agent knows where it lives. Emits ONLY under `POLYROB_LOCAL` or effective `AUTONOMY_MODE=autonomous` — a p…", "internal"),
    ("PROJECT_CONTEXT_MAX_TOKENS", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`20000`", "Token cap on project-context content. F25: at the default the cap instead follows the MODEL WINDOW — `clamp(window * 4%, 4000, 40000)` — and this value is only the fallback when the window is unknown; set it to anything else to PIN the cap. Over budget, the cut keeps head 70% +…", "advanced"),
    ("PROJECT_CONTEXT_SERVER_MODE", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (NOT a safe-local flag)", "Load project context on the server (not local mode) and inject it untrusted-wrapped (framed as DATA, not instructions). Searches the tenant session workspace (`pm().get_workspace_dir`), NEVER the process CWD/install dir. `POLYROB_LOCAL` does NOT flip this on.", "advanced"),
    ("EPISODIC_MEMORY_ENABLED", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (**ON under POLYROB_LOCAL + AUTONOMY_ENABLED, or `AUTONOMY_POSTURE` owner-visible/full**)", "Episodic activity ledger: write one durable, time-ordered row per completed run (chat/goal/cron) to the `episodes` table in `memory.db`, independent of H-MEM findings. Feeds `recent_activity`, the session-start digest, and the continuity bridge.", "advanced"),
    ("EPISODIC_DIGEST_INJECT", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (**ON under POLYROB_LOCAL + AUTONOMY_ENABLED, or `AUTONOMY_POSTURE` owner-visible/full**)", "Inject a passive session-start digest of recent episodes (chat sessions only, `exclude_surfaced=True`) as a pinned foundation message.", "advanced"),
    ("CONTINUITY_BRIDGE_ENABLED", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (**ON under POLYROB_LOCAL + AUTONOMY_ENABLED**)", "Idle-reset continuity bridge: write a closing episode + seed the next session's first step with a short \"what happened last time\" bridge message.", "advanced"),
    ("AUTONOMOUS_CONTINUITY_BRIDGE", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (**ON under `AUTONOMY_POSTURE` owner-visible/full**)", "§7.5: carry a recent-activity summary INTO an autonomous goal/cron tick (mirror-image of the chat digest — autonomous-only, first-step, never sub-agent) so ticks stop re-deriving \"nothing new\". Additive context; fail-open.", "advanced"),
    ("SELF_EVOLUTION_TRANSPARENCY", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (**ON under POLYROB_LOCAL + AUTONOMY_ENABLED**)", "§7.1: proactively notify the owner (Telegram) when the agent writes a pending identity/skill proposal, and back the `polyrob owner pending/promote/reject` surface. Fail-open.", "advanced"),
    ("GOAL_BLOCKER_ESCALATION", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (**ON under `AUTONOMY_POSTURE` owner-visible/full**)", "§7.2: when a goal trips the circuit breaker (`status='blocked'`) OR the planner leaves the pipeline empty repeatedly, surface a concrete ask to the owner over the cron/delivery telegram rail instead of dying silently; also leaves a tracked `kind='ask'` row on the goal board (`po…", "advanced"),
    ("GOAL_EMPTY_PIPELINE_ESCALATE_AFTER", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`2`", "Consecutive planner runs that leave the ready queue EMPTY before the stall is escalated to the owner (rides `GOAL_BLOCKER_ESCALATION`; a \"queue healthy\" planner verdict never escalates; escalates once per stall).", "advanced"),
    ("GOAL_GROUP_MAX_REPLIES_PER_RUN", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`3`", "how many room lines ONE service run (a cron job or goal carrying `payload.group`) may answer. The run is told the number in its rubric and each answer is a `send_message(reply_to=<message id>)`. This is the per-RUN share of the room's hourly ceiling (`GROUP_REPLY_CAP_PER_HOUR`),…", "advanced"),
    ("GOAL_COMPLETION_JUDGE", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "**ON**", "§4.3 evidence-grounded completion review (autonomous runs): a cheap aux model (the `judge` aux slot) reads the agent's CLAIM (done() text) against the mechanical evidence pack — action ledger, artifact diff, captured ids, typed-check results — acceptance prose optional. `unmet`…", "advanced"),
    ("GOAL_JUDGE_TIMEOUT_SEC", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`60`", "Wall-clock bound on one completion-judge LLM call; timeout fails open to pass.", "advanced"),
    ("GOAL_BLOCKED_MAX_AGE_DAYS", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`14`", "§5.3 blocked-goal stewardship: `blocked` goals older than this (measured from when they blocked) age out VISIBLY to `cancelled` (logged `aged_out` event) on the dispatch tick, instead of rotting as permanent planner context. `0` disables aging. The owner/agent can requeue a bloc…", "advanced"),
    ("GOAL_BLOCKED_PROVIDER_RETRY_MIN", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`30` (minutes)", "For typed block kinds, a `blocked` goal whose `payload.block_kind == \"provider_outage\"` (stamped by `dispatcher._fail_run` when the failure classified as an LLM/provider death) is a transient, self-healing block — `age_out_blocked` requeues it (`blocked`→`ready` + `provider_outa…", "advanced"),
    ("REFLECTION_ON_SESSION_CLOSE", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (**ON under `AUTONOMY_POSTURE` owner-visible/full**)", "§7.7: consolidate a short session's findings at session close (the per-step 25-finding trigger is unreachable for short cron/goal sessions). Extra aux-model call per closed session.", "advanced"),
    ("AUTONOMY_STATE_DURABLE", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "ON", "Restart-durable autonomy state (`autonomy_state.db`): background delegations write dispatched/terminal rows (a crash-interrupted delegation is marked `interrupted` at next start and surfaced back to its session — never silently resumed), and the self-wake `ReentryBudget` depth c…", "internal"),
    ("REFLECTION_SESSION_CLOSE_THRESHOLD", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`5`", "Minimum findings a session must accrue for the `REFLECTION_ON_SESSION_CLOSE` trigger to fire (cost gate).", "advanced"),
    ("CONTINUITY_LLM_SUMMARY", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "OFF (everywhere; NOT a safe-local flag)", "Use an aux-model LLM call to summarize the closing episode for the continuity bridge instead of a mechanical summary. Off by default everywhere — adds latency at reset.", "advanced"),
    ("EPISODIC_RETENTION_DAYS", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`90`", "Episodic row retention window (days). Enforced by a global (all-tenants) prune riding the curator's own tick cadence — never the write path.", "advanced"),
    ("AUTONOMY_HEARTBEAT_INTERVAL_SEC", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "`300` (min 30)", "Interval of the autonomy runtime's heartbeat ticker (liveness stamp + event-log maintenance host).", "advanced"),
    ("POLYROB_STREAMS_MANIFEST", "Autonomy & continuous-learning loops", "unset (then `<data_home>/streams/streams.yaml` if it exists; no manifest ships)", "Path override for an operator-authored streams manifest the stream seeder loads. Nothing ships in the package; a fresh install has no standing work until an owner writes one. `load_manifest` refuses a path under a session workspace and the file is hard-denied to agent writes.", "advanced"),
    ("SUB_AGENTS_ENABLED", "Delegation / sub-agents", "**ON** (`'true'`; `BotConfig` field also `True`)", "Enable `delegate_task` / sub-agent delegation.", "public"),
    ("SUBAGENT_LEAST_PRIVILEGE", "Delegation / sub-agents", "ON (`'true'`)", "Give a delegated child a narrowed dedicated controller/toolset.", "advanced"),
    ("DELEGATE_BLOCKED_TOOLS", "Delegation / sub-agents", "`{agent_nft, app_service, code_execution, coding, cronjob, dapp_browser, defi_trade, git, github, hf_deploy, launchpad, mcp, process, publish, self_env, shell, tool_manage, worker_manage, x402_invoice, x402_pay}` plus the enabled packs' rows (`hyperliquid`, `polymarket`, `x_browser`)", "Container tool_ids dropped from a delegated child. Default DERIVED from the capability table and the pack manifests (`ids_with(\"delegate_blocked\")`). The env can only ADD — it is UNIONed with the default (M5, 2026-09-14: it used to REPLACE, so naming one extra tool silently unbl…", "advanced"),
    ("MAX_SUB_AGENT_DEPTH", "Delegation / sub-agents", "`1`", "Delegation depth backstop.", "advanced"),
    ("MAX_CONCURRENT_SUB_AGENTS", "Delegation / sub-agents", "`3`", "Max concurrent sub-agents.", "advanced"),
    ("MAX_ASYNC_SUB_AGENTS", "Delegation / sub-agents", "`2` (clamped ≤ concurrent)", "Background/async delegation slots.", "advanced"),
    ("SUB_AGENT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS", "Delegation / sub-agents", "`600`", "Single sub-agent (`goal`) timeout.", "advanced"),
    ("SUB_AGENT_TIMEOUT", "Delegation / sub-agents", "`600`", "Single sub-agent (`goal`) timeout.", "advanced"),
    ("PARALLEL_SUBTASKS_TIMEOUT_SECONDS", "Delegation / sub-agents", "`900`", "Parallel-subtasks timeout.", "advanced"),
    ("PARALLEL_SUBTASKS_TIMEOUT", "Delegation / sub-agents", "`900`", "Parallel-subtasks timeout.", "advanced"),
    ("WORKERS_ENABLED", "Delegation / sub-agents", "OFF", "043 §6 — arm the tenant-scoped worker (agent-profile) store. A \"worker\" is an `AgentProfileModel` (prompt/llm/tools/limits) authored per tenant under `<data_home>/profiles/user_{uid}/`, threat-scanned (body AND description separately, fail-CLOSED → `.pending/` quarantine), atomi…", "advanced"),
    ("AUTONOMOUS_RIG_DEFAULT", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`full`", "057 WS-A: deploy-wide named tool rig for cron/goal runs — `money_rail` \\", "advanced"),
    ("AUTONOMOUS_TOOL_DISCLOSURE", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF (`false`)", "057 WS-A: pin the `<tool-catalog>` block and register `load_tool` for an AUTONOMOUS session independently of `POLYROB_LOCAL`, so a narrow rig can widen itself mid-run. Money tools stay never-loadable. Which sessions count as autonomous is answered by `agents/task/session_class.p…", "advanced"),
    ("STABLE_AUTONOMOUS_TOOLSET", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "ON (`true`)", "057 WS-A: freeze the REQUESTED autonomous toolset — stop dropping/re-adding `email` on the 900 s SMTP verdict TTL (056 WS4), which flipped the cached prompt prefix (4 distinct tool counts in one prod day). The rejection is told via the tool's `gated:credentials-rejected` catalog…", "advanced"),
    ("TOOL_SCHEMA_STABLE_ORDER", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "ON (`true`)", "057 WS-A: sort the emitted tool schemas by action name once in `get_all_actions_for_provider`, so two registries with the same ids emit identical bytes (the order was dict insertion order, which varies with load order). ON since 2026-09-22; `false` = pre-057 registration order.…", "internal"),
    ("TOOL_SCHEMAS_FROZEN", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF (`false`)", "063 WS-4 (F9), OPT-IN shape (a) — the provider-neutral schema-freeze bridge. The default late-tool path is `grow` (`tools[]` grows on `load_tool`, as before 2026-09-23) or `deferred` on a capable Anthropic model — see `ANTHROPIC_DEFERRED_TOOLS`; the ONE resolver is `modules/llm/…", "advanced"),
    ("ANTHROPIC_DEFERRED_TOOLS", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "ON (`true`)", "063 WS-4 (F9), shape (b) — Anthropic's NATIVE mid-conversation tool changes, the default late-tool path on a capable Anthropic model. A tool registered after the session's first emit is still emitted, carrying `\"defer_loading\": true`: the request knows the tool but the model's c…", "advanced"),
    ("TOOL_CATALOG_TAIL_UPDATES", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "ON (`true`)", "063 WS-4 (F8): keep the FIRST `<tool-catalog>` render as the pinned foundation snapshot and deliver every later status change as ONE durable `<tool-catalog-update>` message at the tail, naming only the tool lines that moved. The catalog carries live gate status and is re-rendere…", "internal"),
    ("FOUNDATION_REPLAY", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "ON (`true`)", "063 WS-6 (F13): on a session reload, replay the foundation blocks PERSISTED in `message_history.json` (system prompt, runtime identity, `<environment>`, self context, project context, initial task, skill catalog, tool catalog) and the tool-name emit order, instead of re-renderin…", "internal"),
    ("SELF_CONTEXT_COMBINED", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF (`false`)", "060 WS-1: the self-context foundation tier is pinned as its DECLARED blocks — awareness, SOUL, owner rules (`owner.md`), operating contract + style line, SELF doc — one `SELF_CONTEXT` message per non-empty block, so the owner's rules are capped, dated and reported apart from the…", "internal"),
    ("AUTONOMOUS_READ_PAGE_LINES", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`0` (off)", "057 WS-B: default page (lines) for an UNPAGED `read_file`. Applied only when the caller named no window at all (no offset/limit/char_offset/char_limit); the header states the page and how to read more. An explicit window always wins.", "advanced"),
    ("VERDICTS_DB_PATH", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "unset (`<data_home>/verdicts.db`)", "057 WS-F: override the durable external-rail verdict store (standing SMTP 535 / X-API 402 / missing-key refusals with `first_seen`/`last_seen`/`count`, shared by every unit on the data dir; fail-open to an in-process dict). Mainly a test seam so verdicts stay out of the develope…", "internal"),
