    ("APP_SERVICE_NGINX_CONF_DIR", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`/etc/nginx/apps.d`", "Where the supervisor writes one `<slug>.conf` per live app. Your wildcard nginx server block must `include` this directory.", "advanced"),
    ("APP_SERVICE_SOURCE_ROOT", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "unset", "An extra directory (beyond the data home and the supervisor's cwd) an app's source dir may live under; the supervisor refuses to snapshot from anywhere else.", "advanced"),
    ("APP_SERVICES_DB_PATH", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`<data_root>/app_services.db`", "Override for the app registry DB (tests redirect it per test).", "advanced"),
    ("AGENT_BUILDER_MODE", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`off`", "The FIFTH named default bundle (032; the `AUTONOMY_MODE` precedent): `off` = byte-identical; `build` = `PUBLISH_ENABLED` + `GITHUB_TOOL_ENABLED` default ON and `publish` joins the autonomous goal toolset; `ship` = `build` + `APP_SERVICE_ENABLED` + `APP_SERVICE_ALLOW_PUBLIC` ON a…", "public"),
    ("SELF_ENV_ENABLED", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF (**ON at `AGENT_COMPUTE_POSTURE>=2`**)", "Register the `self_env` self-maintenance tool (install_dep/read_source/patch_source/git_pull/restart_service). Every verb is `compute_posture_allows(ctx,2)`- AND approval-gated; install-tree-confined; env/config hard-denied. In `DELEGATE_BLOCKED_TOOLS`.", "advanced"),
    ("POLYROB_INSTALL_TREE", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "repo root (2 levels up from `tools/self_env/tool.py`)", "The install-tree root `self_env` read/patch/git_pull operate under (realpath-confined). Set to `/opt/polyrob` on prod.", "advanced"),
    ("HF_DEPLOY_ENABLED", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF (not safe-local)", "Register the `hf_deploy` tool (deploy/undeploy/list_deployments — publish the session workspace as a Hugging Face Space, Docker SDK). Requires `compute_posture_allows(ctx,2)`. The FIRST publish of a new app needs the owner's approval through the provider the Controller resolves…", "advanced"),
    ("HF_DEPLOY_ORG", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "unset", "The Hugging Face org/user namespace to publish Spaces under (`<HF_DEPLOY_ORG>/<app_name>`). Required for `deploy`/`undeploy`; refused with a clear error when unset.", "advanced"),
    ("HF_DEPLOY_DAILY_MAX", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`10`", "Max deploy attempts per tenant per rolling 24h.", "advanced"),
    ("HF_DEPLOY_MIN_INTERVAL_SEC", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`120`", "Minimum seconds between deploy attempts of the SAME app.", "advanced"),
    ("OBJECTIVE_GOAL_BUDGET", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`25`", "Max LIVE (non-cancelled) goals one objective may have attached. Past the cap `GoalBoard.create` REFUSES a new child with a message telling the agent to finish/cancel open goals or raise an ask instead — an objective is allowed to be standing, not infinite. An objective's own `pa…", "advanced"),
    ("PUBLISH_ENABLED", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF (not safe-local; ON under `AGENT_BUILDER_MODE=build\\", "ship`)", "advanced"),
    ("PUBLISH_ROOT", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`<data_home>/publish`", "Directory the web server serves publications from. Approved slugs live at `<PUBLISH_ROOT>/<slug>/`; unapproved ones wait under `<PUBLISH_ROOT>/.pending/<slug>/`, which is not a valid slug and so is unreachable — the approval gate is enforced by the filesystem layout, not by appl…", "advanced"),
    ("PUBLISH_BASE_URL", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "unset (relative URLs)", "Public base URL that serves `PUBLISH_ROOT` (e.g. `https://pub.example.com`). The `publish` tool returns `<PUBLISH_BASE_URL>/<slug>/`; unset yields a relative `/<slug>/`, which is honest but not shareable. Set it to the public vhost that serves `PUBLISH_ROOT`.", "advanced"),
    ("PUBLICATIONS_DB_PATH", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`<data_root>/publications.db`", "Override the publications DB location (slug → status/url/size). Mainly a test seam.", "internal"),
    ("ARTIFACTS_DB_PATH", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`<data_root>/artifacts.db`", "Override the artifact-ledger DB location (one row per file the agent produces: producer, path, sha256, size, kind, published url). Mainly a test seam.", "internal"),
    ("HF_TOKEN", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "unset (secret)", "Hugging Face fine-grained write token used ONLY by the `hf_deploy` broker (`HfApi`) to create/update Spaces and set secrets; read+stripped at call time, never logged/returned (broker errors are token-scrubbed). See the owner runbook in `docs/guide/self-hosting.md`.", "advanced"),
    ("DEPLOYED_APPS_DB_PATH", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "unset (derived from data root)", "Override path for the `hf_deploy` registry DB (`deployed_apps.db`); the test suite redirects this to keep unit runs off the developer's real data home.", "advanced"),
    ("CRON_ENABLED", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF (ON under `AUTONOMY_POSTURE=full`, which is the posture default under effective `AUTONOMY_MODE=autonomous`)", "Register the `cronjob` tool + start the cron ticker. `cronjob_schedule` accepts a genuine owner turn in every regime, and a goal/cron-dispatched main-agent run on the owner tenant only when the money regime is `autonomous` or `armed`; a leaf, self-wake, delegation-result, room o…", "public"),
    ("WAKE_CHANGE_GATE", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF (**ON under `AUTONOMY_POSTURE=full`**)", "Cron wake change-gate: a job with `payload.change_gated` skips the paid model call ($0 tick, `cron_run skipped/no_change`) when the tenant's observable state fingerprint (goal board/events, other cron runs, newest episode) is unchanged since the last tick. Delivery jobs (`payloa…", "advanced"),
    ("MESSAGE_TOOL_ENABLED", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF (**ON under POLYROB_LOCAL**)", "Agent-callable `message(surface, target, text, action)` send tool. Every non-owner target is default-DENIED unless owner-allowlisted (`polyrob owner allow <surface> <target>` / Telegram `/allow`). ⚠️ Owner-target resolution reads the single process-level operator env (`POLYROB_O…", "advanced"),
    ("MESSAGE_AUTONOMOUS_ALLOWLISTED", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF (ON under `AUTONOMY_MODE=autonomous`)", "Whether a forged/AUTONOMOUS turn (goal/cron/planner session, sub-agent, self-wake re-entry) may use `message` at all. OFF = blanket refusal (\"owner must be in the loop\"). ON = the send falls through to the normal tier gate, so an autonomous run can reach ONLY the owner or an own…", "advanced"),
    ("OWNER_MESSAGE_COOLDOWN_SEC", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`7200` (2h)", "Minimum gap an autonomous/forged turn (goal/cron/planner session, sub-agent, self-wake re-entry) must respect before proactively messaging the OWNER again — checked against the durable conversation store's REAL send history, never the model's own self-report of elapsed time. `<=…", "advanced"),
    ("DELIVERABLES_ATTACH_ENABLED", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF (**ON under POLYROB_LOCAL + AUTONOMY_ENABLED**)", "Goal/cron completion pushes attach the run's file deliverables (screened + capped) to the OWNER chat via the delivery rail; the honest text listing (`attached` / `server-only: <path> (<reason>)`) rides regardless. Owner rail only — correspondents never receive workspace files.", "advanced"),
    ("DELIVERABLES_ATTACH_MAX_MB", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`10`", "Per-file attach cap in MB for the completion AUTO-attach (Telegram bot API hard limit is 50). Oversized files are listed server-only, never silently dropped. The explicit `message` tool rides the larger `MESSAGE_MEDIA_MAX_MB` instead.", "advanced"),
    ("DELIVERABLES_ATTACH_MAX_FILES", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`3`", "Max files attached to one completion message; the remainder is listed by name+size+path.", "advanced"),
    ("DELIVERABLES_MAX_LINES", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`5`", "UNCONDITIONAL cap on individually-listed deliverable lines in one owner message; everything past it becomes ONE roll-up line plus the console link (chat-first review 2026-08-22, G1/G4). Attached and published files are never rolled up. This bound does NOT depend on ledger attrib…", "advanced"),
    ("MESSAGE_MEDIA_MAX_MB", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`45`", "Per-file cap for the explicit `message` tool `media_paths` send (owner-directed; Telegram hard limit ~50 MB). The full attach screen (confinement, secret filename+content, injection scan) applies regardless of cap.", "advanced"),
    ("INBOUND_MEDIA_ENABLED", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "ON", "Master switch for the INBOUND media rail: a photo/document/video arriving on a chat surface is stored in the session workspace under `inbound/` and described on the turn (image ⇒ a vision block, small text file ⇒ inlined, anything else ⇒ referenced by path). OFF = no file is sto…", "advanced"),
    ("INBOUND_MEDIA_MAX_MB", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`20`", "Per-file cap for a file arriving from a chat surface. Over the cap the file is not stored and the turn says so.", "advanced"),
    ("INBOUND_MEDIA_MAX_FILES", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`5`", "Max attachments read from ONE inbound message; the remainder is counted on the turn (\"N more attachment(s) … were not read\"), never dropped in silence.", "advanced"),
    ("INBOUND_IMAGE_MAX_MB", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`10`", "Per-image cap for building a vision block (base64 inflates ~33%). Over the cap the image IS stored and its path named, but no vision block is built — the agent is told to say so rather than guess.", "advanced"),
    ("WEBVIEW_PUBLIC_URL", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "unset", "Public base URL of the owner-auth webview console (e.g. `https://console.example.com`). Set ⇒ goal completions carry a `/session/<id>` deep link and the daily digest a console line; unset ⇒ no links (byte-identical). Links carry no credentials — the console's own owner login gat…", "public"),
    ("APPROVAL_REQUIRED_TOOLS", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`''` (no-op)", "Comma list of tools requiring approval before execution.", "advanced"),
    ("APPROVAL_PROVIDER", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`auto`", "Approval provider: `auto`(allow)/`auto_notify`(allow + `tool_auto_approved` audit event + post-hoc owner notification — act-and-report)/`deny`/custom (`interactive_cli`, `owner_queue` self-register on import). Under effective `AUTONOMY_MODE=autonomous` an unset/`auto`/`interacti…", "public"),
    ("APPROVAL_TIMEOUT_SEC", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`30`", "Approval-request timeout (cancels provider on expiry). The generic 30s default applies only to in-process providers; every durable `owner_queue` wait (payment lanes AND the non-payment queued lanes, 030 WS-E2) defaults to the remote-round-trip 300s via `approval_wait_timeout_sec…", "advanced"),
    ("PAYMENT_APPROVAL_MODE", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`approve` (`auto` under `AUTONOMY_MODE=autonomous`)", "the owner-legible switch for outward payment-creation actions (`PAYMENT_APPROVAL_TOOLS`), gated FIRST-CLASS independent of `APPROVAL_REQUIRED_TOOLS`. `approve`: every request (receive AND spend) queues through the durable, remote-capable `owner_queue` provider (`tools/controller…", "public"),
    ("APPROVAL_GRANT_TTL_HOURS", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`24`", "TTL for an `owner_queue` ONE-SHOT grant: an owner decision recorded AFTER the requester already timed out still lets the NEXT identical request (same tool+params+tenant hash) through without re-queuing — but only within this window, and only once (atomic single redemption via `G…", "advanced"),
    ("POLYROB_TOOL_DENYLIST", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`''`", "Comma list of tools vetoed by the pre-tool-call guardrail (fail-closed).", "advanced"),
    ("POLYROB_AGENT_TOOLSET", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "unset", "Named toolset driving the CLI session's tool list (`resolve_toolset`), same as `polyrob run --toolset <name>`. Unset ⇒ the legacy CLI default list (`filesystem`/`task`/`web_fetch` + gated `coding`/`anysite`). Either way the list is intersected with `cli_unavailable_tools` so unr…", "public"),
    ("TOOL_SCHEMA_ERROR_POLICY", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`DROP_TOOL`", "Invalid native schema handling: `DROP_TOOL`/`RAISE`/`WARN`.", "advanced"),
    ("TOOL_SCHEMA_SANITIZE", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "ON (`'true'`)", "Fix hostile JSON-Schema constructs in the emitted tools list.", "advanced"),
    ("UNTRUSTED_TOOL_RESULT_WRAP", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "**ON**", "Frame untrusted tool-result strings in `<untrusted_tool_result>` delimiters.", "advanced"),
    ("ENABLE_GIF_CREATION", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF", "(Legacy/dead) GIF creation.", "advanced"),
    ("SCREENSHOT_JPEG_QUALITY", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`70`", "JPEG quality (1-95) for the session screenshots written to disk.", "advanced"),
    ("FS_REALPATH_CONFINE", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "ON (`\"on\"`)", "Confine filesystem ops via realpath.", "advanced"),
    ("BROWSER_ALLOW_PRIVATE_URLS", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "OFF (`'false'`)", "Allow browser navigation to private/loopback URLs only for explicit `1/true/yes/on`; unknown values keep protection enabled.", "advanced"),
    ("BROWSER_CDP_URL", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "unset", "Chrome DevTools Protocol endpoint of a browser running as its OWN principal (`polyrob browser install` → `polyrob-browser.service`, `http://127.0.0.1:9222`). REQUIRED once the wallet is enabled: a custody process refuses to launch Chromium and only connects. Every session gets a…", "advanced"),
    ("BROWSER_WSS_URL", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "unset", "Playwright-server WebSocket endpoint of a remote browser (`ws://<private-ip>:3000/<token>`), for a browser on a SECOND host; requires the same Playwright version on both ends. Preferred over CDP across a network (CDP has no authentication). Same fresh-context and never-rendered…", "advanced"),
    ("GIT_TOOL_TIMEOUT_SEC", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`120`", "Per-command subprocess timeout (seconds) for the `git` tool.", "advanced"),
    ("GITHUB_TOKEN", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "unset (secret, masked)", "GitHub token for the `github` tool when no per-user OAuth token is stored (`GITHUB_TOKEN` wins; the standard gh-CLI/Actions names).", "public"),
    ("GH_TOKEN", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "unset (secret, masked)", "GitHub token for the `github` tool when no per-user OAuth token is stored (`GITHUB_TOKEN` wins; the standard gh-CLI/Actions names).", "internal"),
    ("TWITTER_WRITE_MAX_PER_HOUR", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`15`", "Durable hourly attempt cap shared by X API and browser clients across tools and workers in the same data home. Threads reserve every tweet; DMs also consume their separate DM cap. Unreadable budget refuses writes.", "public"),
    ("TWITTER_DM_MAX_PER_HOUR", "Tools / code-exec / cron / approvals", "`5`", "Durable hourly attempt cap for X DMs, reserved on top of `TWITTER_WRITE_MAX_PER_HOUR` in the same budget store; `0` or less refuses every DM. Unreadable budget refuses the DM.", "advanced"),
    ("OPENAI_COMPAT_API_ENABLED", "API / server / sessions", "OFF", "Mount the OpenAI-compatible `/v1` router. On `/v1`, the request `body.model` (which OpenAI SDK clients always send) is applied per-session and overrides the operator's `CHAT_MODEL`/`CHAT_PROVIDER` pin for that session (live `swap_model` on a reused session; baked into the Sessio…", "public"),
    ("MCP_SERVE_ENABLED", "API / server / sessions", "OFF", "Mount the inbound MCP server surface — `POST /mcp`, hand-rolled JSON-RPC-over-POST (not the `mcp` PyPI SDK), auth via the same `X-API-KEY`/JWT/x402 policy as A2A. Lets an MCP client (Claude Desktop, Cursor) call five tenant-safe read-only tools (`rob_usage_summary`, `rob_goals_l…", "advanced"),
    ("SESSION_REGISTRY_BACKEND", "API / server / sessions", "`memory`", "Active session→orchestrator map backend: `memory` (in-proc) or `sqlite` (cross-proc metadata). ⚠️ `sqlite` on BOTH units is the precondition for a WRITABLE console (`WEBVIEW_READ_ONLY=false`): with `memory` the console's own in-process agent cannot see the sessions the agent ser…", "advanced"),
    ("API_AUTH_TOKEN", "API / server / sessions", "unset", "The operator's machine-to-machine SERVICE token. Send it as `X-Service-Token` (the old `X-API-KEY` spelling still works for one release with a one-time WARN). It authenticates as role `service`: full feature access and no per-request 402, but it is NOT admin — `/api/admin/*` ref…", "public"),
    ("API_RATE_LIMIT_RPM", "API / server / sessions", "`60`", "API requests/minute.", "advanced"),
    ("API_RATE_LIMIT_RPH", "API / server / sessions", "`1000`", "API requests/hour.", "advanced"),
    ("API_RATE_LIMIT_BURST", "API / server / sessions", "`10`", "API burst allowance.", "advanced"),
    ("CORS_ALLOW_ORIGINS", "API / server / sessions", "**Two independent consumers, two different defaults** — see note below", "Comma-separated allowed CORS origins.", "advanced"),
    ("WEBVIEW_DOMAIN", "API / server / sessions", "the reference deployment's public host (`webview/server.py`, `api/auth_endpoints.py`); `localhost:5050` (`agents/task/utils_webview.py`) — **inconsistent default across call sites; set `WEBVIEW_DOMAIN` for your own deployment**", "The public hostname this instance is served from. Feeds the Socket.IO CORS default (below) and the SIWE `domain` field (`api/auth_endpoints.py:108`).", "advanced"),
    ("JWT_SECRET_KEY", "API / server / sessions", "unset (dev)", "JWT signing secret, shared by the API auth middlewares and the WebView (`webview/owner_auth.py` issues/verifies the owner session cookie with the same secret). Required in production — `api/app.py` raises `RuntimeError` at startup if unset and `ENVIRONMENT=production`; in dev, u…", "public"),
    ("A2A_BASE_URL", "API / server / sessions", "the reference deployment's base URL (set this to your own public URL)", "Base URL advertised in the A2A agent card.", "advanced"),
    ("WEBVIEW_ACTIVITY_ENABLED", "API / server / sessions", "`true`", "The console's global `/activity` stream (page + `/api/activity/*` + `join_activity` socket room). Owner/admin-gated in every non-local posture, so on-by-default is safe; `false` = 404/denied everywhere.", "advanced"),
    ("WEBVIEW_ACTIVITY_TAIL_SEC", "API / server / sessions", "`2.0`", "Poll interval for the activity hub's SQLite id-cursor tails (`telemetry_events.db`, `goal_events`, `skill_install_audit`). Feed events are push (watchfiles), not polled.", "advanced"),
    ("WEBVIEW_READ_ONLY", "API / server / sessions", "`false`", "Monitoring-only console: every mutating endpoint returns 403 server-side through ONE dependency (`webgate.read_only_guard`; the auth surfaces `/owner-login` and `/api/auth/*` stay reachable so the owner can still log in to LOOK) and the chat input is not rendered. The posture fo…", "advanced"),
    ("POLYROB_API_BASE", "API / server / sessions", "`http://127.0.0.1:9000`", "Base URL of the main task API the webview proxies to (chat delivery, queue-status, health) in the classic two-service shape. Override for a non-default API port/host.", "advanced"),
    ("SESSION_TTL_SECONDS", "API / server / sessions", "`86400`", "Session lifetime.", "advanced"),
    ("MAX_SESSIONS_IN_MEMORY", "API / server / sessions", "`100`", "Resident session cap.", "advanced"),
    ("MAX_SESSIONS_PER_USER", "API / server / sessions", "`10`", "Per-user session cap.", "advanced"),
    ("CREATED_SESSION_TTL_SECONDS", "API / server / sessions", "`3600`", "TTL for a created-but-not-yet-run session.", "advanced"),
    ("SESSION_RESET_MODE", "API / server / sessions", "`idle` (#7)", "Chat session-boundary policy: `idle`/`daily`/`both`/`none`. Default `idle` everywhere — a chat idle past `SESSION_IDLE_MINUTES` starts fresh (memory recall bridges the gap). The server flip (was `none`) is gated on the recreate-race (#2) + mute-on-resume (#0) fixes. Pin `none` f…", "advanced"),
    ("SESSION_IDLE_MINUTES", "API / server / sessions", "`1440` (**720 POLYROB_LOCAL**)", "Idle threshold; a chat idle longer than this starts a fresh session (when `SESSION_RESET_MODE` includes idle). Last-activity is bumped per message via `SessionChatRegistry.touch`.", "advanced"),
    ("SESSION_RESET_HOUR", "API / server / sessions", "`4`", "Local hour (0-23) for the daily session roll (when mode includes daily).", "advanced"),
    ("SURFACE_GC_ENABLED", "API / server / sessions", "ON when local **+** chat bus on, else OFF", "Periodic GC (hourly via the autonomy runtime) of stale chat<->session bindings; horizon `max(2× idle window, 7d)`. Keeps the routing map from growing unboundedly.", "advanced"),
    ("UVICORN_HOST", "API / server / sessions", "`127.0.0.1`", "Uvicorn bind host (read in `main.py`).", "advanced"),
    ("UVICORN_PORT", "API / server / sessions", "`9000`", "Uvicorn bind port (read in `main.py`).", "advanced"),
    ("UVICORN_WORKERS", "API / server / sessions", "`1`", "Uvicorn worker count (read in `main.py`).", "advanced"),
    ("UVICORN_RELOAD", "API / server / sessions", "OFF (`false`)", "Uvicorn auto-reload (read in `main.py`).", "advanced"),
    ("UVICORN_FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS", "API / server / sessions", "`127.0.0.1`", "Which proxies `polyrob serve` trusts for `X-Forwarded-For`/`X-Forwarded-Proto`. Default = the local nginx only; never `*` on a bound port (any direct caller could then claim `127.0.0.1`).", "advanced"),
    ("ENVIRONMENT", "API / server / sessions", "`development` (varies by site)", "Environment selector.", "advanced"),
    ("ENV", "API / server / sessions", "`development` (varies by site)", "Environment selector.", "advanced"),
    ("LOG_LEVEL", "API / server / sessions", "`INFO`", "Logging level.", "public"),
    ("POLYROB_LOG_FILE", "API / server / sessions", "per entrypoint (`bot.log` / `email.log` / `webview.log`)", "Basename of the rotating log file under `<data_home>/logs/`; overrides the per-entrypoint default. Directory components are ignored.", "advanced"),
    ("CHAT_TOOL_IDS", "API / server / sessions", "`task`", "Tools loaded for the chat surface.", "advanced"),
    ("CHAT_MAX_STEPS", "API / server / sessions", "`8`", "Max agent steps for a chat-surface turn.", "public"),
    ("RUN_BUDGET_USD", "API / server / sessions", "`0` (disabled)", "Session-cumulative provider-spend ceiling in USD; when > 0 the run loop halts honestly (`run_budget_exhausted`) before the next step once summed `usage_records.api_cost_usd` for the session reaches the cap. Real provider cost, not the markup user price. Sub-agents ride the paren…", "public"),
    ("CHAT_SKIP_CREDIT_CHECK", "API / server / sessions", "ON (truthy)", "Skip the credit check on chat-path turns.", "advanced"),
    ("API_SECRET", "API / server / sessions", "unset (secret, masked)", "Secret key for the legacy `AuthenticationMiddleware` on the API app (`API_SECRET` wins, `ADMIN_TOKEN` is the fallback name); unset = that middleware is not added.", "advanced"),
    ("ADMIN_TOKEN", "API / server / sessions", "unset (secret, masked)", "Secret key for the legacy `AuthenticationMiddleware` on the API app (`API_SECRET` wins, `ADMIN_TOKEN` is the fallback name); unset = that middleware is not added.", "advanced"),
    ("PRODUCTION", "API / server / sessions", "OFF (`'true'` enables)", "Marks the deploy as production independent of `ENV`: a missing `JWT_SECRET_KEY` then becomes a fatal startup error instead of a dev warning.", "advanced"),
    ("SESSION_LLM_LIMIT", "API / server / sessions", "`5` (min 1)", "Per-session concurrent-LLM-call semaphore in the orchestrator.", "advanced"),
    ("MAX_QUEUED_MESSAGES", "API / server / sessions", "`10`", "Per-session HITL inbound message queue bound (overflow is refused).", "advanced"),
    ("DOC_CLAIM_PROVENANCE_REQUIRED", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "OFF (`false`)", "057 WS-D: arm the identity-doc claim guard — a NEW or CHANGED line in `owner.md`/`self.md` that matches the claim lexicon (`lacks", "advanced"),
    ("POLYROB_LOCAL", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "OFF", "Single-user terminal profile; flips the `_SAFE_LOCAL_FLAGS` group ON as a default.", "public"),
    ("ROB_LOCAL", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "OFF", "Legacy alias for `POLYROB_LOCAL` (either being truthy enables local mode), kept so old docs/env files are not a silent no-op. Retire after 1.4.", "internal"),
    ("POLYROB_DATA_DIR", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "unset", "Isolation switch (doc 01/06): when set — the headless/server case — the runtime data home (goals.db/cron.db/memory.db + agent workspaces) lives THERE, OUTSIDE the code tree, and the workspace is under it (not cwd). Unset (local-dev): the data home is `<POLYROB_HOME>/data` (`~/.p…", "public"),
    ("POLYROB_PROJECT_DIR", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "unset", "When set, the agent uses this folder as ONE persistent workspace shared across sessions/goals/cron (Claude-Code style), independent of `POLYROB_DATA_DIR`. Also via `polyrob --project <path>`. Goal concurrency is clamped to single-flight while active; the cross-process lock keys…", "advanced"),
    ("POLYROB_LOG_DIR", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "unset", "Runtime log directory override. Unset → `<data_home>/logs`; it never writes into the installed code tree. Never CWD-relative.", "advanced"),
    ("POLYROB_PROJECT_SECRET_REFUSE", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "`0`", "When truthy, refuse to start if the cwd-default persistent workspace contains secrets/`.git` (SEC-1). Default = warn only.", "advanced"),
    ("POLYROB_REQUIRE_PAIRING", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "OFF", "Owner-allowlist + DM-pairing ingress gate; when ON, an unpaired sender or unreadable pairing store is denied at the surface dispatcher; unused pairing codes expire after 15 minutes.", "advanced"),
    ("TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "unset", "Telegram bot token (from @BotFather) for the `polyrob telegram` local-polling surface. Read from process env or `~/.polyrob/.env` (`polyrob config set`; the CLI does not load a project `.polyrob/.env`); never commit it.", "public"),
    ("ALLOWED_TELEGRAM_USER_IDS", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "unset", "Comma list of raw Telegram numeric user ids allowed to drive the bot. Unset ⇒ bot is locked and replies with the sender's id (bootstrap); set ⇒ only those ids reach the agent, others are ignored. A single entry here also serves as the owner tg id when `POLYROB_OWNER_TELEGRAM_ID`…", "public"),
    ("POLYROB_OWNER_TELEGRAM_ID", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "unset", "The owner's raw Telegram numeric id, used for two things: (1) the inbound owner alias — an inbound from this id is aliased to the OWNER principal (`POLYROB_OWNER_USER_ID`) instead of its surface-hashed `u_…` id, so the owner's chat shares autonomy's tenant (goals/memory/SELF); (…", "public"),
    ("POLYROB_OWNER_EMAIL", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "unset", "The owner's email address for out-of-band cron delivery (`deliver=\"email\"`) on single-owner headless deploys where no `user_directory` service is registered. Mirrors `POLYROB_OWNER_TELEGRAM_ID`. Unset ⇒ email delivery has no recipient (fail-open, no send). Requires `CRON_DELIVER…", "public"),
    ("BOT_OWNER_EMAIL", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "unset", "The owner's email address for out-of-band cron delivery (`deliver=\"email\"`) on single-owner headless deploys where no `user_directory` service is registered. Mirrors `POLYROB_OWNER_TELEGRAM_ID`. Unset ⇒ email delivery has no recipient (fail-open, no send). Requires `CRON_DELIVER…", "internal"),
    ("OWNER_SURFACE", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "unset (= `telegram`)", "030 WS-B1: the owner-notice fan-out order for `deliver_user_message` (approvals, credit sentinel, goal-blocked, settlement, cron reports) — a comma list of surface ids, primary first (e.g. `slack,telegram`). Each entry resolves an address via `owner_address()` (user_directory →…", "public"),
    ("OWNER_SURFACES", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "unset (= `telegram`)", "030 WS-B1: the owner-notice fan-out order for `deliver_user_message` (approvals, credit sentinel, goal-blocked, settlement, cron reports) — a comma list of surface ids, primary first (e.g. `slack,telegram`). Each entry resolves an address via `owner_address()` (user_directory →…", "internal"),
    ("OWNER_<SURFACE>_ID", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "unset", "The owner's address on that surface for the `OWNER_SURFACE` fan-out (mirrors `POLYROB_OWNER_TELEGRAM_ID`/`POLYROB_OWNER_EMAIL`, which telegram/email keep using). `SURFACE` is the surface catalog's `owner_env`: `SLACK`, `DISCORD`, `SIGNAL`, `WHATSAPP`, `X`, `DINGTALK` (the owner'…", "public"),
