    ("GROUP_REPLY_CAP_PER_HOUR", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "`20`", "max committed replies `MessageRouter.publish` sends into one room chat per rolling hour; over cap the reply is suppressed (logged, never queued) and never counted twice. Read via a COUNT over `room_events`, so a restart can't reset it. DMs are never gated. A room that sets `chat…", "advanced"),
    ("GROUP_MEMBER_COOLDOWN_SEC", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "`20`", "minimum seconds between two triggers from the SAME sender (human or bot) in one room chat; a trigger inside the window is refused (`route_inbound` DENIED, silent). A room that sets `chat.member_cooldown_sec` overrides this for itself; `0` disables the cooldown for that room.", "advanced"),
    ("GROUP_BOT_LOOP_MAX", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "`20`", "max bot-authored triggers allowed in one room chat within `GROUP_BOT_LOOP_WINDOW_SEC`; the limit-th+ trip records a `bot_loop_trip` and every further bot trigger is refused until `GROUP_BOT_LOOP_COOLDOWN_SEC` elapses. Humans are never counted here.", "advanced"),
