    ("CLI_SUPPRESS_DONE_RECAP", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "ON (`\"true\"`)", "Suppress the duplicate `done()` recap bubble after the streamed reply in `polyrob run` (mirrors the REPL); `off` restores the legacy double bubble. Retire after 1.4.", "internal"),
    ("CLI_TODO_DOT_ROB", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "ON (`\"true\"`)", "In a project-root workspace, keep the agent TODO file under `.polyrob/` instead of the project root.", "advanced"),
    ("CLI_TODO_SESSION_SCOPED", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "ON (`\"true\"`)", "Per-session TODO file under `.polyrob/` (session-scoped) instead of the legacy single shared `<project>/.polyrob/todo.md`. Retire after 1.4.", "internal"),
    ("CONFIG_ENV", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "unset (→ `ENV` → `development`)", "Highest-precedence spelling of the environment name that selects `config/.env.<env>` (`CONFIG_ENV` > `ENV` > `development`; see the env-files section at the top).", "advanced"),
    ("POLYROB_INSTANCE_ID", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "`\"polyrob\"` (`DEFAULT_INSTANCE_ID`; in profile mode the active profile name)", "Instance identity id; `POLYROB_INSTANCE_ID` is canonical, `BOT_INSTANCE_ID` an accepted alias. `BOT_INSTANCE_ID` retire after 1.4.", "public"),
    ("BOT_INSTANCE_ID", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "`\"polyrob\"` (`DEFAULT_INSTANCE_ID`; in profile mode the active profile name)", "Instance identity id; `POLYROB_INSTANCE_ID` is canonical, `BOT_INSTANCE_ID` an accepted alias. `BOT_INSTANCE_ID` retire after 1.4.", "internal"),
    ("POLYROB_OWNER_USER_ID", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "unset → **`local`**", "Explicit binding of this instance's OWNER principal (an internal `user_id` — not a raw Telegram id). It is the tenant key the owner's chat/CLI operates under. You normally do NOT set this: precedence is (1) this var, (2) first `SURFACE_SUPER_ADMIN_USER_IDS`, (3) the owner tenant…", "public"),
    ("BOT_OWNER_USER_ID", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "unset → **`local`**", "Explicit binding of this instance's OWNER principal (an internal `user_id` — not a raw Telegram id). It is the tenant key the owner's chat/CLI operates under. You normally do NOT set this: precedence is (1) this var, (2) first `SURFACE_SUPER_ADMIN_USER_IDS`, (3) the owner tenant…", "internal"),
    ("POLYROB_LOCAL_OWNER", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "unset", "Fallback owner tenant id, ranked BETWEEN an explicitly-bound owner and the unbound default `local` (uses the strict `resolve_owner_principal(default_to_instance=False)` so it isn't shadowed by the auto-derive). ⚠️ It is read by the ONE owner-tenant resolver, so setting it moves…", "advanced"),
    ("SURFACE_SUPER_ADMIN_USER_IDS", "Identity / polyrob / local profile", "unset", "Comma list of internal `user_id`s. Only its FIRST entry has any effect — it is precedence (2) for the OWNER principal (`resolve_owner_principal`). POLYROB's model is single-owner: there is no surface-layer role ladder, so entries 2..N are inert. (The dead `SurfacePermissions` la…", "advanced"),
    ("PREFS_ENABLED", "Preferences (owner UX)", "ON", "Master switch for the whole preferences layer; when OFF, `resolve_with_source` always returns the env/default value and `preferences.toml` is never read.", "advanced"),
    ("PREFS_TOOL_ENABLED", "Preferences (owner UX)", "OFF (**ON under POLYROB_LOCAL**)", "Agent-callable `preferences(operation, key?, value?, text?)` action — `list`/`get` read the typed schema (effective value/source/applies); `set` writes SAFE keys immediately or queues a pending proposal for GUARDED keys (owner reviews with `/pending`); `contract_propose` propose…", "advanced"),
    ("CONTRACT_DOC_ENABLED", "Preferences (owner UX)", "ON", "Injects the owner-authored operating-contract doc (`contract.md`, legacy; `preferences(contract_propose)` writes the owner RULES doc instead, so no NEW `contract.md` is created — this flag only keeps an EXISTING one injected) plus a deterministic one-line style summary from type…", "internal"),
    ("CONTRACT_DOC_REQUIRE_REVIEW", "Preferences (owner UX)", "ON (retained for existing drafts)", "⚠️ No longer governs a write. `contract_propose` now records into the owner RULES doc (`owner.md`), whose activation requires separate owner review — one rule instead of a per-doc flag. Retained only so an EXISTING `contract.md` draft stays listable/promotable for one release; `…", "advanced"),
    ("FINANCIAL_CLAIM_GATE_ENABLED", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "**ON**", "022 send-time gate: an outbound message (`message`, `send_message`, `email_send`, `twitter_post`/`reply`/`quote`/`thread`/`dm`, `x_post`/`x_reply`/`x_dm`) whose text claims money moved (paid / earned / received / settled + an amount or a money noun) is REFUSED, by name (`refused…", "advanced"),
    ("BILLING_FAILOVER_ENABLED", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "**ON**", "Attempt provider fallback on a billing/quota/402 error before permanent halt. Detection is the SSOT `core/credit_sentinel.py::looks_like_credit_death` (I-5, 2026-07-10 — the old ad-hoc substring check missed real-shape 402s). On a single-funded-provider deployment there is nothi…", "advanced"),
    ("CREDIT_SENTINEL_ENABLED", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "**ON**", "§6.3 provider-credit sentinel: a credit-death refusal (402/insufficient_quota/billing) from an autonomous goal/cron run sends ONE safety-net notice via the delivery rail and pauses goal dispatch + LLM cron ticks via a durable latch file (`<data_root>/CREDIT_SENTINEL`) — ends the…", "advanced"),
    ("CREDIT_SENTINEL_RELEASE_HOURS", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`6`", "Auto-release window for the credit sentinel — after this many hours the latch expires and one paid probe may run (re-tripping if credits are still dead). Remove the latch file to release early.", "advanced"),
    ("LLM_OUTAGE_NOTICE", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "**ON**", "When an owner-facing chat-surface turn dies with ALL LLM providers exhausted (e.g. the 2026-07-16 OpenRouter 402 cascade), send ONE static, LLM-independent ⚠️ notice back over the originating surface instead of total silence. Classification reuses the credit-death SSOT plus prov…", "advanced"),
    ("X402_ENABLED", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "OFF (`'false'`)", "Enable x402 pay-per-request *receiving*.", "public"),
    ("X402_CLIENT_ENABLED", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "OFF (`'false'`)", "Enable the agent-side x402 *paying* tool.", "advanced"),
    ("X402_PAYMENT_RECIPIENT", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`''`", "Treasury/recipient address for x402 receipts. Explicit value always wins; when EMPTY, `resolve_treasury_address()` falls back to the agent wallet's treasury address (see `X402_TREASURY_FROM_WALLET`).", "advanced"),
    ("X402_TREASURY_FROM_WALLET", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "**ON**", "when `X402_PAYMENT_RECIPIENT` is empty and the agent wallet is enabled, the wallet's treasury-venue address is used as the x402 receive address — read from memory at call time, never written to any env file. Inert on a default deploy (`AGENT_WALLET_ENABLED` is OFF). One-time WAR…", "advanced"),
    ("X402_INVOICE_ENABLED", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "OFF (ON under `AUTONOMY_MODE=autonomous`)", "Agent money loop: registers the `x402_invoice` tool (`x402_request` create-invoice + `x402_invoices` list + `accounting` unified ledger) AND starts the settlement watcher in the autonomy runtime. Needs `X402_PAYMENT_RECIPIENT`. `x402_request` is in the recommended approval set;…", "advanced"),
    ("X402_INVOICE_MAX_USD", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`50`", "Hard ceiling on a single agent-created payment request (an absurd invoice is a reputation incident).", "public"),
    ("FAIL_ON_INSUFFICIENT_CREDITS", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "ON", "Billing enforcement mode of the usage tracker: ON = an LLM call that would overdraw the tenant's credits raises `InsufficientCreditsError` and stops the run (fail-fast billing); OFF = the call is recorded but not blocked (dev/reconciliation only). Strict `true` match on purpose…", "advanced"),
    ("X402_INVOICE_DAILY_MAX", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`10`", "Max invoices one tenant may create per trailing 24h.", "advanced"),
    ("X402_PUBLIC_RATE_PER_WINDOW", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`20`", "G-20: per-IP call budget for the PUBLIC (anon-allowed, enumerable `inv_<12hex>` id) invoice endpoints — `GET /api/x402/requests/{id}` and `POST /api/x402/requests/{id}/pay`. Reuses the existing generic sliding-window limiter (`tools/mcp/rate_limit.py::MCPExecRateLimiter`, same m…", "advanced"),
    ("X402_PUBLIC_RATE_WINDOW_SEC", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`60`", "Window (seconds) for `X402_PUBLIC_RATE_PER_WINDOW`.", "advanced"),
    ("X402_TRUSTED_PROXIES", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`''` (loopback `127.0.0.1`/`::1` always trusted)", "⚠️ Security fix (G-20 regression, reproduced live): the public invoice rate limiter above was keyed on `get_client_ip`, which returns a client-supplied `X-Forwarded-For` VERBATIM — spoofable, letting an attacker either evade the cap (rotate a fake XFF per request) or poison a vi…", "advanced"),
    ("USAGE_INVOICE_BRIDGE_ENABLED", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "OFF", "the metering→invoice bridge: registers the read-only `usage_summary` agent action (tenant-scoped LLM usage rollup — api_cost_usd/credits/calls, optionally narrowed to a `session_id`/`since` — plus a non-binding `suggested_invoice` draft). Fixes G-29 (`LLMUsageTracker.get_session…", "advanced"),
    ("USAGE_INVOICE_MARKUP", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`1.0`", "Multiplier applied to a rollup's `api_cost_usd` when `build_invoice_draft` proposes a `suggested_invoice` amount (`1.0` = passthrough, no markup). A distinct flag from `PRICING_MARKUP` (`modules/credits/pricing.py`) — that one prices internal platform credit-billing; this one pr…", "advanced"),
    ("INVOICE_CARD_ENABLED", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "OFF (**ON under POLYROB_LOCAL, or when `X402_INVOICE_ENABLED` is on**)", "after a successful `x402_request`, also render a branded PNG invoice card (the agent avatar, else the brand mark; amount, purpose, request id, expiry, \"billed to\" when `payer_contact` is present, QR, pay instructions, footer) into the session workspace (`<workspace>/invoices/inv…", "advanced"),
    ("INVOICE_QR_STYLE", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`address`", "What the invoice card's QR code encodes (via `modules/x402/artifact.py::build_payment_artifact`): `address` — the bare treasury address string (works with any wallet's \"scan an address\" import); `eip681` — an EIP-681 USDC transfer URI (`ethereum:<usdc_contract>@<chain_id>/transf…", "advanced"),
    ("X402_SETTLEMENT_WATCH_INTERVAL_SEC", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`60`", "Settlement-watcher tick interval (expire stale invoices; wake the originating session via self-wake when one settles; emits `payment_settled`/`payment_expired`).", "advanced"),
    ("X402_SETTLE_ONCHAIN_DETECT", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "OFF (ON under `AUTONOMY_MODE=autonomous`)", "the settlement watcher ADDITIONALLY scans the treasury address for plain USDC `Transfer` logs (no facilitator, no `POST /pay`) and auto-settles the matching PENDING agent invoice by exact amount — so a human payer who just sends USDC to the address the invoice instructions show…", "advanced"),
    ("X402_INVOICE_AMOUNT_JITTER", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "**ON**", "Amount-collision jitter for on-chain matching: when a colliding equal-amount PENDING invoice already exists for the same treasury, `create_payment_request` nudges the new amount by a deterministic sub-cent increment (never exceeding `X402_INVOICE_MAX_USD`) so on-chain amount-mat…", "internal"),
    ("X402_SETTLEMENT_SCAN_MAX_SPAN", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`5000`", "Max blocks one settlement-watcher tick will scan for on-chain detection, even after a long gap (bounds a single `eth_getLogs` call). Only consulted when `X402_SETTLE_ONCHAIN_DETECT` is on.", "advanced"),
    ("X402_SETTLEMENT_CONFIRMATIONS", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`2`", "Confirmations buffer for on-chain detection — blocks within this many of the chain head are never scanned yet (a just-mined block can still reorg out). Only consulted when `X402_SETTLE_ONCHAIN_DETECT` is on.", "advanced"),
    ("X402_SETTLEMENT_RPC", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`''`", "watcher-specific RPC pin for on-chain detection, any chain — beats `DEFI_EVM_RPC_BASE` (which the scan now also honors on mainnet, parity with balance reads) and the built-in defaults (`https://mainnet.base.org` / `https://sepolia.base.org`).", "advanced"),
    ("PAYMENT_DEFAULT_ASSET", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`''` (⇒ the chain's canonical USDC)", "046: instance-wide default `asset_id` for a new invoice when the caller names none. An unknown id is a REFUSAL that echoes the known ids — never a fallback to another asset, because an invoice quoted in the wrong token is money sent to a contract nobody is watching.", "advanced"),
    ("PAYMENT_QUOTE_MAX_AGE_SEC", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`300`", "046: max age of a price quote used to size a USD-denominated invoice in a NON-stable asset. A staler quote is refused rather than used. Inert until a quoter is registered (the initial paid-actions implementation).", "advanced"),
    ("ROOM_ACTIONS_ENABLED", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "OFF", "paid moderation actions in a group room. A member may buy a moderation effect in a room whose owner enabled and priced it (`chat.paid_enabled` + `chat.paid_<verb>_usd`). OFF = a member's `/mute` is REFUSED, never priced. ⚠️ It needs `X402_INVOICE_ENABLED` (which starts the settl…", "advanced"),
    ("ROOM_ACTION_OFFER_TTL", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`30m`", "046: fallback deadline for an UNPAID paid-action offer, for a room that set no `chat.paid_offer_ttl`. The room's own value always wins, and the INVOICE is minted with the same deadline so a payer can never pay an expired offer.", "advanced"),
    ("ROOM_ACTION_CARD_ENABLED", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "⇒ `ROOM_ACTIONS_ENABLED`", "046 phase 2: render a payment card (QR) alongside a paid-action offer and deliver it in the room. Deliberately NOT `INVOICE_CARD_ENABLED`, which defaults OFF on a server — reusing it would mean no deployment that can host a room ever renders a QR. Fail-open: a render fault costs…", "advanced"),
    ("SUBSCRIPTIONS_ENABLED", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "OFF", "the first revenue wedge: watchtower subscriptions — a prepaid-period + renewal-invoice model gating a cron job's continued firing. Driven entirely from the EXISTING settlement-watcher tick (no new ticker): each tick creates renewal invoices ahead of `paid_through` (respecting `P…", "advanced"),
    ("WATCHTOWER_PRICE_USD", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`10.00`", "Default monthly price (USD) for a watchtower subscription — `create_subscription` falls back to this when no explicit `amount_usd` is given.", "advanced"),
    ("SUBSCRIPTION_RENEWAL_LEAD_DAYS", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`5`", "Days before a subscription's `paid_through` the settlement watcher creates the next renewal invoice.", "advanced"),
    ("SUBSCRIPTION_GRACE_DAYS", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`3`", "Days past `paid_through` a lapsed subscription keeps its cron job running (status `grace`, still chasing renewal) before it is `suspended` (cron job $0-skips).", "advanced"),
    ("X402_DEFAULT_CHAIN", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`base`", "Default chain for x402.", "advanced"),
    ("X402_FACILITATOR_URL", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`''`", "x402 facilitator endpoint.", "advanced"),
    ("X402_PRICE_USD", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "_derived_ (unset ⇒ economics-based, ~$30)", "Single-source x402 per-request price — the middleware charge, `/api/x402/pricing`, the Agent Card, and the 402 challenge all read this. If set, it wins. If unset (or invalid), the price is DERIVED: `X402_MAX_TOKENS_PER_REQUEST × max-model-output-rate × X402_PRICE_MARKUP` — the w…", "advanced"),
    ("X402_MAX_TOKENS_PER_REQUEST", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`200000`", "Token budget one x402 request prepays for. SSOT for BOTH the derived price AND the runtime hard cap — `LLMUsageTracker` halts an x402 request (`InsufficientCreditsError`) once its per-session cumulative tokens exceed this, so actual cost can never exceed what was prepaid (S6 cos…", "advanced"),
    ("X402_PRICE_MARKUP", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`2.0`", "Safety multiplier on the derived x402 price (margin over worst-case token cost). Ignored when `X402_PRICE_USD` is set.", "advanced"),
    ("AGENT_WALLET_ENABLED", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "OFF", "Enable the agent's native wallet.", "public"),
    ("AGENT_WALLET_MASTER_SEED", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "unset — **SECRET, masked**", "The agent wallet's master seed (hex, ≥32 chars); every wallet key derives from it. `polyrob wallet init` writes it to `~/.polyrob/.env`; `polyrob doctor`/`wallet` verbs read it to check wallet health. Distinct from `PAYMENT_MASTER_SEED` (deposit-address derivation, below). Seed…", "advanced"),
    ("AGENT_WALLET_NETWORK", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`testnet`", "Wallet network (`testnet`/`mainnet`).", "public"),
    ("AGENT_WALLET_BACKEND", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`local_eoa`", "Wallet key backend.", "advanced"),
    ("AGENT_WALLET_MAX_PER_TX_USD", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`250`", "Per-transaction USD ceiling (catastrophic-loss guard, NOT a budget). Hardened down from `1000000`, then from `1000` (H3, 2026-08-22: $1000 in one transaction is not \"catastrophe-only\" on this treasury). This env value is the DEFAULT: an owner-approved `budget.wallet_per_tx_usd`…", "public"),
    ("AGENT_WALLET_OPERATIONAL_VENUE", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`treasury`", "Venue key that same-chain spend paths (x402, generic payments) SIGN with, so the funded address (`AgentWallet.address`) equals the spent-from address. \"Venue\" elsewhere stays a policy/accounting label; hyperliquid keeps its own delegated key.", "advanced"),
    ("WALLET_SIGNER", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`local`", "066 P2: where the agent's signatures come from. `local` = today: the agent process holds the seed and signs in process. `shadow` = it still signs locally AND asks `polyrob-signer` (its own UID, Unix socket `/run/polyrob-signer/signer.sock`, `SO_PEERCRED`-checked) for a verdict o…", "public"),
    ("AGENT_WALLET_DERIVATION", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "unset (`meta.json` wins; absent = legacy)", "Recovery-hatch override for the wallet's key-derivation scheme (`legacy` \\", "advanced"),
    ("WALLET_DAILY_CAP_USD", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`100`", "Rolling 24h spend cap (H3, 2026-08-22: was unset/disabled — the per-tx ceiling alone cannot stop a within-ceiling loop draining the treasury one ticket at a time). Set `none`/`off`/`unlimited`/`disabled` to restore the old unbounded behaviour explicitly; a set-but-unparseable va…", "public"),
    ("CREDIT_VALUE_USD", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`0.01`", "USD value of one credit.", "advanced"),
    ("WELCOME_BONUS", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`0`", "Optional new-wallet credit grant; default zero because wallet creation does not prove a unique person. A positive value deliberately subsidizes repeat wallet signups.", "advanced"),
    ("EIP8004_ENABLED", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "OFF (`'false'`)", "Enable EIP-8004 on-chain agent registration.", "advanced"),
    ("EIP8004_PAYMENT_FEEDBACK", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "OFF", "the ERC-8004 ⇄ x402 compose seam: on settlement of an invoice with an identifiable payer (`correspondent_ref`, an ACTIVE correspondent channel) AND a verifiable on-chain transaction hash, offer that payer a signed ERC-8004 feedback authorization + `ProofOfPayment` (built via `mo…", "advanced"),
    ("EIP8004_ONCHAIN_ENABLED", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "OFF (`'false'`)", "Operator ATTESTATION that this agent is registered on an Identity Registry someone else transacted with: flips the publicly-served `/eip8004/registration.json` `trustMode` from `local` to `onchain`, and (only when `EIP8004_AGENT_ID`/`EIP8004_IDENTITY_REGISTRY` are also set) emit…", "advanced"),
    ("EIP8004_AGENT_PRIVATE_KEY", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "unset — **SECRET, mask in logs/exports**", "Signing key for ERC-8004 EIP-712 feedback authorizations (`ReputationManager`). This is a second, independent signing key — it is NOT derived from `AGENT_WALLET_MASTER_SEED` and has no relationship to the agent wallet's PBKDF2 derivation tree. Consequence: the wallet migration p…", "advanced"),
    ("EIP8004_CHAIN_ID", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`8453` (Base)", "Chain id the ERC-8004 registries live on.", "advanced"),
    ("EIP8004_IDENTITY_REGISTRY", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "unset", "Contract addresses of the three ERC-8004 registries; unset = that registry is unconfigured (local/simulation mode).", "advanced"),
    ("EIP8004_REPUTATION_REGISTRY", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "unset", "Contract addresses of the three ERC-8004 registries; unset = that registry is unconfigured (local/simulation mode).", "advanced"),
    ("EIP8004_VALIDATION_REGISTRY", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "unset", "Contract addresses of the three ERC-8004 registries; unset = that registry is unconfigured (local/simulation mode).", "advanced"),
    ("EIP8004_AGENT_ID", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`0` (= none)", "This agent's on-chain ERC-8004 agent id; `0`/unset = not registered.", "advanced"),
    ("EIP8004_AGENT_WALLET", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "unset", "The wallet address attested in the ERC-8004 registration (an address, not a key).", "advanced"),
    ("EIP8004_SUPPORTED_TRUST", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`reputation`", "Comma list of trust models advertised in `/eip8004/registration.json`.", "advanced"),
    ("IPFS_GATEWAY", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`https://ipfs.io/ipfs/`", "IPFS gateway base URL for ERC-8004 metadata resolution.", "advanced"),
    ("ETHEREUM_RPC_URL", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "unset", "Per-chain JSON-RPC endpoints for ERC-8004 contract calls (chain ids 1/8453/137/42161); unset = on-chain 8004 calls for that chain are unavailable. Distinct from the DeFi rail's `DEFI_EVM_RPC_<CHAIN>` pins.", "advanced"),
    ("BASE_RPC_URL", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "unset", "Per-chain JSON-RPC endpoints for ERC-8004 contract calls (chain ids 1/8453/137/42161); unset = on-chain 8004 calls for that chain are unavailable. Distinct from the DeFi rail's `DEFI_EVM_RPC_<CHAIN>` pins.", "advanced"),
    ("POLYGON_RPC_URL", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "unset", "Per-chain JSON-RPC endpoints for ERC-8004 contract calls (chain ids 1/8453/137/42161); unset = on-chain 8004 calls for that chain are unavailable. Distinct from the DeFi rail's `DEFI_EVM_RPC_<CHAIN>` pins.", "advanced"),
    ("ARBITRUM_RPC_URL", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "unset", "Per-chain JSON-RPC endpoints for ERC-8004 contract calls (chain ids 1/8453/137/42161); unset = on-chain 8004 calls for that chain are unavailable. Distinct from the DeFi rail's `DEFI_EVM_RPC_<CHAIN>` pins.", "advanced"),
    ("CDP_API_KEY_ID", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "unset (secret is masked)", "Coinbase CDP credentials for the mainnet x402 facilitator (from portal.cdp.coinbase.com); testnet's x402.org facilitator needs neither.", "advanced"),
    ("CDP_API_KEY_SECRET", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "unset (secret is masked)", "Coinbase CDP credentials for the mainnet x402 facilitator (from portal.cdp.coinbase.com); testnet's x402.org facilitator needs neither.", "advanced"),
    ("X402_PAYMENT_ADDRESS", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "unset", "Legacy env spelling for the x402 receive address, kept as the LAST fallback after `resolve_treasury_address()` (explicit `X402_PAYMENT_RECIPIENT` > wallet treasury > this).", "advanced"),
    ("ADMIN_WALLETS", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "unset", "Comma list of wallet addresses granted the admin tier under SIWE/wallet auth (case-insensitive compare).", "advanced"),
    ("OWNER_WALLET_ADDRESSES", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "unset", "Comma list of the owner's OWN receive addresses (EVM `0x…` or Solana base58). A genuine owner chat turn that transfers to one of these, or to the agent's own wallet, waits on no second owner tap; caps and `tx_guard` still apply. File-only (the console cannot write it).", "advanced"),
    ("PRICING_MARKUP", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`1.00`", "Multiplier on provider API cost for internal credit billing (`1.20` = +20%). Distinct from `USAGE_INVOICE_MARKUP` (outbound agent invoices).", "advanced"),
    ("MIN_CREDIT_CHARGE", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`1`", "Minimum credits charged per LLM call (prevents free calls).", "advanced"),
    ("SESSION_CREATION_COST", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`1`", "Credits charged for creating a session.", "advanced"),
    ("VISION_CALL_COST", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`2`", "Credits charged per vision call.", "advanced"),
    ("TOOL_CALL_COST", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`0.5`", "Credits charged per tool call.", "advanced"),
    ("DEN_SIGNUP_ALLOWANCE", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`2000`", "One-time DEN sign-up credit allowance per token id (keyed per token to prevent transfer abuse).", "advanced"),
    ("ETH_PRICE_USD_OVERRIDE", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "unset", "Fixed ETH/USD price for the deposit monitor — bypasses the live CoinGecko fetch entirely. For ops/testnets with no real price feed; never set on a mainnet deployment (it would misprice real deposits).", "advanced"),
    ("ETH_PRICE_USD_MAX", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`50000`", "Sanity upper bound on the ETH/USD price (override or live fetch); a price above this raises instead of crediting a wildly-inflated deposit — guards against an oracle schema error or an `ETH_PRICE_USD_OVERRIDE` typo.", "advanced"),
    ("DEPOSIT_MONITOR_ENABLED", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "OFF", "Enable the deposit-monitoring background loop (requires `SEPOLIA_RPC_URL`/`ETHEREUM_RPC_URL` too).", "advanced"),
    ("TREASURY_SWEEPER_ENABLED", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "**OFF**", "Master gate for `TreasurySweeper` — the SaaS-deposit-side component that signs and broadcasts real fund-moving transactions, sweeping per-user deposit-address balances into the treasury. Before this flag existed the sweeper started on config presence alone (`TREASURY_ADDRESS` +…", "advanced"),
    ("TREASURY_ADDRESS", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "unset", "Gnosis Safe / treasury wallet address the sweeper moves swept funds to. One of the three config-presence conditions `TreasurySweeper` checks — inert on its own without `TREASURY_SWEEPER_ENABLED=true` and a resolved master seed.", "advanced"),
    ("SWEEP_INTERVAL", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "`3600` (1h)", "Poll interval (seconds) between `TreasurySweeper` sweep passes, once enabled.", "advanced"),
    ("ENABLE_AUTH", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "OFF", "The real billing gate. `core/initialization.py::initialize_auth_services()` (called unconditionally from `core/bot.py` on every boot) returns immediately when this is `False`, *before* `balance_manager`/`tier_manager`/`api_key_manager`/`wallet_generator`/the deposit monitor are…", "advanced"),
    ("PAYMENT_MASTER_SEED", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "unset", "Master seed for deterministic per-user deposit-address derivation. Two names have existed historically (`PAYMENT_MASTER_SEED` is the documented convention; `MASTER_SEED` is a legacy pydantic-settings alias) — `resolve_master_seed()` is the SSOT: `PAYMENT_MASTER_SEED` wins if set…", "advanced"),
    ("MASTER_SEED", "Billing / x402 / wallet", "unset", "Master seed for deterministic per-user deposit-address derivation. Two names have existed historically (`PAYMENT_MASTER_SEED` is the documented convention; `MASTER_SEED` is a legacy pydantic-settings alias) — `resolve_master_seed()` is the SSOT: `PAYMENT_MASTER_SEED` wins if set…", "internal"),
    ("DEFI_DATA_ENABLED", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "ON", "the read-only `defi_data` tool (verbs incl. `nft_holdings`/`nft_info` under `NFT_TOOLS_ENABLED`): `token_resolve` (candidate contract addresses for a ticker), `token_info` (on-chain identity + price + liquidity + safety screen), `price`, `swap_quote` (prices a swap through the s…", "advanced"),
    ("DEFI_TRADE_ENABLED", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "OFF", "the `defi_trade` tool's EVM money verbs: `transfer`, `approve_token` (exact-amount only), `revoke_approval`, `swap` (route seam: local Uniswap V3 first, `DEFI_ROUTE_AGGREGATOR` fallback). This one can move real funds. (`solana_swap` arms separately via `SOLANA_TRADE_ENABLED`.) E…", "public"),
    ("DEFI_MAX_SLIPPAGE_BPS", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "`100`", "Default (clamped to 1–1000) slippage bound for `defi_trade.swap`, in basis points (100 = 1%). A fill worse than this REVERTS on-chain rather than executing at a bad price. A caller may pass a tighter or looser `slippage_bps` per swap (1–1000). How it is enforced differs by route…", "public"),
    ("DEFI_ROUTE_DRIFT_MAX_PCT", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "`3.0`", "Maximum disagreement between a swap quote and independent prices, also used to value bridge arrival floors. EVM and Solana swaps check the executable minimum against independently priced input value, allowing this drift plus the declared slippage. A measured held-token exit may…", "advanced"),
    ("DEFI_ROUTE_AGGREGATOR", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "(unset = off)", "names a DEX aggregator to consult when local construction finds no pool. Accepts `lifi`; unset/`none`/`off`/`false`/`0` (the default) means no aggregator, and an unknown name is refused rather than guessed at, so a typo cannot silently arm or disarm a money path. Why it exists:…", "advanced"),
    ("DEFI_PORTFOLIO_PRICE_BUDGET_SEC", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "`40`", "Wall-clock ceiling on the PER-HOLDING half of `defi_data.portfolio` (EVM path) — identity resolution AND pricing — in seconds. ⚠️ Must stay below the controller's 60 s per-action timeout (`TOOL_TIMEOUTS['default']`), with room to render: it was `120` until 2026-09-24, which mean…", "advanced"),
    ("DEFI_AUTONOMOUS_MAX_USD", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "`25`", "Per-transaction ceiling below which a `defi_trade` verb may execute autonomously; above it `tx_guard` returns `lane=owner_queue` and does NOT execute. Bounded in turn by the PolicyGate per-tx ceiling and the rolling daily cap, whichever is lower (so also by the signer envelope).…", "public"),
    ("DEFI_TIERED_SPEND_LANE", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "OFF", "An explicit owner-controlled mode. `defi_trade`'s four verbs sit on `PAYMENT_APPROVAL_TOOLS`' SPEND lane, which queues them through `owner_queue` in every mode; unattended, that tap never comes and the trade times out. ON: a live spend whose declared `max_spend_usd` is within `D…", "advanced"),
    ("X402_AUTONOMOUS_MAX_USD", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "`1.0`", "Per-payment ceiling below which an `x402_fetch` skips the owner-approval tap and runs act-and-report. Above it the payment goes to the durable `owner_queue`. Autonomous runs also require an explicit `WALLET_VENUE_DAILY_CAP_X402_USD`; successful payments emit the shared owner not…", "public"),
    ("DEFI_AUTONOMOUS_TURN_TRADING", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "OFF", "narrows `tx_guard`'s turn-origin bar. Step 2 of `authorize` refuses ANY turn `_is_forged_or_autonomous_turn` flags, which is right for a leaf/sub-agent, a self-wake and a delegation-result re-entry — but a goal/cron-dispatched run is also \"autonomous\", so with this OFF (the defa…", "advanced"),
    ("DEFI_MONITOR_EXITS", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "OFF", "2026-08-26 exit untying — lets a forged main-agent turn (self-wake / delegation-result: the monitor loop) execute EXIT-shaped operations that `DEFI_AUTONOMOUS_TURN_TRADING`'s stricter detector refuses. A week of prod logs showed stop rules firing on monitor ticks and the turn-or…", "advanced"),
    ("DEFI_EVM_RPC_BASE", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "`https://mainnet.base.org`", "Operator-pinnable JSON-RPC endpoint for Base, used by every on-chain read (`core/wallet/onchain.py`, `defi_data`, the x402 settlement scan). The default is the shared public endpoint, which is unauthenticated and rate-limited; pinning a real one stops a provider hiccup from degr…", "advanced"),
    ("DEFI_EVM_RPC_<CHAIN>", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "per-chain public endpoint", "The same pin for every OTHER chain in `core/wallet/chains.py`: `DEFI_EVM_RPC_ETHEREUM`, `DEFI_EVM_RPC_ARBITRUM`, `DEFI_EVM_RPC_POLYGON`, `DEFI_EVM_RPC_ROBINHOOD`, `DEFI_EVM_RPC_OPTIMISM` (Optimism is a READ-only row, `money_enabled=False`: a pin there speeds reads and arms nothi…", "advanced"),
    ("ALCHEMY_API_KEY", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "unset (secret, masked)", "Alchemy API key: unlocks the Alchemy per-chain RPC fallback for on-chain reads (`rpc_url_for_chain`, when no `DEFI_EVM_RPC_<CHAIN>` pin) and the token-balance index `defi_data.portfolio` needs to enumerate EVM holdings (without it portfolio reports `coverage: partial`).", "advanced"),
    ("DEFI_SOLANA_RPC", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "`https://api.mainnet-beta.solana.com`", "Operator-pinnable Solana JSON-RPC, used by `defi_data.portfolio` on the `solana` chain (native SOL + SPL enumeration). The default is the shared public endpoint, which is heavily rate-limited — pin a real one (Helius, Triton) before relying on it. A failed read renders UNKNOWN,…", "advanced"),
    ("POSITION_LEDGER_PATH", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "(unset = `<POLYROB_PROJECT_DIR>/kb-root-position-ledger.md`)", "Where the LIVE position ledger lives, so the status surfaces can report how many positions the agent believes it holds. The treasury figure is CASH FLOW (income − spend) and structurally cannot see a held bag; before 2026-08-28 `/status` said only \"open positions NOT included\",…", "advanced"),
    ("DEFI_AGENT_AUTONOMY", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "OFF", "Owner directive 2026-09-12 — adds the on-chain rail (`defi_data`, `defi_trade`, and since 042 `launchpad` + `dapp_browser`) to the autonomous grant, so the agent can reach DeFi without a per-action owner hand-off. Applies to all three consumers of that grant: the owner's interac…", "advanced"),
    ("DEFI_BRIDGE_ENABLED", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "OFF", "arms `defi_trade.bridge`, the cross-chain move, through Relay.link (chosen because LI.FI's own answer for Solana -> Robinhood Chain is `tool: relaydepository`, i.e. Relay; going through LI.FI would add a layer whose route choice we cannot pin to reach the settlement network we c…", "advanced"),
    ("DEFI_DEPLOY_ENABLED", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "OFF", "arms `defi_trade.deploy_token` and `defi_trade.deploy_contract`, the CREATE transaction. A create is the one shape the guard's delta model did not cover: no destination, no counterparty, and the thing it produces does not exist until it does. What is asserted instead, all BEFORE…", "advanced"),
    ("NFT_TOOLS_ENABLED", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "OFF", "The non-fungible verbs: `defi_data.nft_holdings` / `nft_info` (read) and `defi_trade.nft_transfer` / `nft_revoke_approval` (write). There is deliberately NO grant verb — `setApprovalForAll(operator,true)` is refused by `tx_guard` for every transaction and is not expressible anyw…", "advanced"),
    ("EIP8004_REGISTER_ENABLED", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "OFF", "The ERC-8004 identity write verbs — `defi_trade.register_agent` (mints this agent's own identity token on the pinned Identity Registry) and `defi_trade.set_agent_uri` (updates the published registration file). ⚠️ Gates the VERBS only: `tx_guard`'s registration receipt assertion…", "advanced"),
    ("EIP8004_AGENT_URI_MODE", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "`auto`", "Where the ERC-8004 registration file lives: `auto` (a hosted URL when `A2A_BASE_URL` is a public host, else a base64 `data:` URI), `data` (always inline — needs no hosting at all, which is what the spec recommends), or `hosted` (refuse unless a public URL exists). An oversized d…", "advanced"),
    ("DEFI_LIQUIDITY_ENABLED", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "OFF", "Arms Uniswap v3 `lp_add`, `lp_remove`, `lp_collect` on Robinhood, Base and Ethereum, and Uniswap v4 `lp_add` (`protocol='v4'`: a new full-range position on a Pons graduated PoolKey, Robinhood only). Dry-run by default. Reads remain available. Guard checks two asset legs, pinned…", "advanced"),
    ("LP_ETH_CAP", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "`0`", "The LP program cap, in ETH: the most native a v4 `lp_add` may have sent in total, summed from the durable spend ledger (`native_raw` on every booked v4 `lp_add`; the declared maximum, so the sum over-counts the SWEEP refund, never under-counts). `0` refuses every v4 native depos…", "advanced"),
    ("LP_ETH_DAILY_CAP", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "`2`", "Rolling-24h bound, in ETH, on the same sum (090 R4). `0` = no daily bound beyond `LP_ETH_CAP`.", "advanced"),
    ("LP_ETH_FLOOR", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "`0.5`", "The native balance, in ETH, a v4 `lp_add` must leave in the wallet (090 R4 ETH floor).", "advanced"),
    ("UNISWAP_V3_POSITION_MANAGER_<CHAIN>", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "pinned", "Optional confirmation of the pinned v3 manager; a different address refuses. CHAIN is ROBINHOOD, BASE or ETHEREUM.", "advanced"),
    ("UNISWAP_V4_POSITION_MANAGER_<CHAIN>", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "pinned", "Optional confirmation of the pinned v4 manager; cannot override it. Does not arm v4 writes.", "advanced"),
    ("DEFI_CALL_ENABLED", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "OFF", "arms `defi_trade.call`, the GENERIC contract write: the agent supplies its own ABI-encoded calldata, so a protocol nobody integrated ahead of time becomes usable. This is what the Aave MCP was missing — that server prepares UNSIGNED transactions and never holds a key, which is w…", "advanced"),
    ("AGENT_NFT_ENABLED", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "OFF", "arms the `agent_nft` tool (050, 069 v4): act through an agent NFT — an ERC-721 whose ERC-6551 token-bound account holds assets — that this instance OWNS on its own treasury address (a human transfers it in, mints it to the treasury, or the agent mints it; `agent_nft_snapshot` /…", "advanced"),
    ("VALUELESS_CHAIN_MONEY", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "OFF", "C13: arms money on a `valueless` testnet chain row — today only Robinhood Chain TESTNET (46630) — for a core run there before mainnet. With it the row is money-enabled; `tx_guard` prices its native coin and wrapped native at exactly $0 (no source prices testnet ETH, and an unpri…", "advanced"),
    ("AGENT_NFT_REVEAL_MAX_GAS_USD", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "`1.00`", "The most USD of gas FEE one `agent_nft_collection_reveal` transaction may cost (`reveal(ids)` on a pinned collection profile with the `reveal` capability; `reveal(10)` measured 369,566 gas). `tx_guard`'s `is_collection_reveal` shape prices the WORST-case fee (simulated gas × 1.5…", "internal"),
    ("LAUNCHPAD_ENABLED", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "OFF", "arms the `launchpad` tool (`launchpad_launch` / `_buy` / `_sell` / `_quote` / `_status`) against Pons V2 on Robinhood Chain, the chain's dominant token launchpad. A launchpad is neither a deploy nor a swap: it is a create-and-seed in ONE transaction against a protocol we did not…", "advanced"),
    ("DAPP_BROWSER_ENABLED", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "OFF", "arms the `dapp_browser` tool (`dapp_connect` / `dapp_status` / `dapp_disconnect`), which injects an EIP-1193 provider (plus the EIP-6963 announcement modern dapps actually listen for) into the session's existing browser context. The gap it closes: the agent could read any dapp a…", "advanced"),
    ("TX_NOTIFY_SENT_HOLD_SEC", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "`60`", "seconds the BROADCAST (`⛓ SENT`) line waits for its own settlement before going to the owner alone. The EVM verbs settle inside the call that broadcast, so SENT and CONFIRMED landed together — six critical-lane DMs for one $1.60 exit (approve/swap/revoke × 2, 2026-09-21). A sett…", "advanced"),
    ("TX_NOTIFY_ENABLED", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "`true`", "the ONE money-execution notice rail (`core/wallet/tx_notify.py`). Every broadcasting `defi_trade` verb (swap, solana_swap, transfer, approve/revoke, bridge) sends the owner two messages per transaction: a BROADCAST notice the moment the transaction is accepted (verb, chain/route…", "internal"),
    ("WALLET_CONTEXT_VISIBLE", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "`true`", "the agent sees its OWN balances in every turn's `<live-health>` note, not just when it remembers to call `defi_data.portfolio`. A new typed `wallet` section in `core/status_snapshot.py` renders native ETH per money chain (Base, Robinhood, Arbitrum, Ethereum), SOL, and USDC where…", "advanced"),
    ("BRIDGE_WATCHER_ENABLED", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "follows `DEFI_BRIDGE_ENABLED`", "the reconciliation ticker for in-flight bridges (`core/wallet/bridge_watcher.py`, every 120s on the autonomy runtime). `await_arrival` parks an unresolved bridge `in_flight` after 300s and returns; until this, that was the LAST thing that ever happened to the row — nothing re-me…", "advanced"),
    ("DEFI_SOLANA_SIM_MAX_ACCOUNTS", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "`5`", "How many accounts `simulateTransaction` may be asked state for on the Solana money path. Measured, not theoretical (2026-09-11, prod): `getMultipleAccounts` allows 100, but the pinned RPC (Alchemy) refuses more than 5 — `{'code': -32602, 'message': 'Too many accounts provided; m…", "advanced"),
    ("SOLANA_TRADE_ENABLED", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "OFF", "arms `defi_trade.solana_swap`, the first Solana path that can move value. Default OFF, so shipping the rail changes nothing until an operator sets it. One verb, not three: Jupiter needs no standing delegate, so the EVM `approve -> swap -> revoke` cycle has no meaning on Solana.…", "advanced"),
    ("DEFI_SOLANA_PROGRAM_ALLOWLIST_EXTRA", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "unset (empty)", "Extra Solana program ids (comma-separated base58) a `solana_swap` transaction may call at TOP LEVEL, on top of the built-in set (System, ComputeBudget, SPL Token, Token-2022, Associated-Token, the SPL memo programs and the Jupiter v4/v6 aggregator programs). The transaction byte…", "advanced"),
    ("X402_SOLANA_SETTLE", "DeFi / on-chain trading", "OFF", "arms the watcher's Solana settlement pass, ANDed with `X402_SETTLE_ONCHAIN_DETECT`. Its own flag on purpose: arming EVM detection must not silently arm a second chain's money path, which has a different rail, a different signer family and a different matching strategy. That stra…", "advanced"),
    ("POLYROB_POSTURE", "WebView / Console (deployment posture, owner login, branding)", "_derived_ (see below)", "Explicit deployment posture override: `local` \\", "public"),
    ("WEBGATE_MULTITENANT", "WebView / Console (deployment posture, owner login, branding)", "OFF", "Back-compat boolean alias that maps onto `POLYROB_POSTURE=multitenant` when the explicit posture var is unset (step 1 of the resolution order above). `polyrob dashboard --posture` and `--multitenant` are the CLI-facing spellings. Retire after 1.4.", "internal"),
    ("WEBGATE_HOST", "WebView / Console (deployment posture, owner login, branding)", "_posture-derived_ (`127.0.0.1` for `local`, `0.0.0.0` for `own_ops`/`multitenant`)", "Explicit bind-host override; also feeds posture derivation (step 2 above) when `POLYROB_POSTURE`/`WEBGATE_MULTITENANT` are both unset — a non-loopback value implies `own_ops`. `WEBGATE_HOST` wins over `WEBVIEW_HOST` when both are set.", "advanced"),
    ("WEBVIEW_HOST", "WebView / Console (deployment posture, owner login, branding)", "_posture-derived_ (`127.0.0.1` for `local`, `0.0.0.0` for `own_ops`/`multitenant`)", "Explicit bind-host override; also feeds posture derivation (step 2 above) when `POLYROB_POSTURE`/`WEBGATE_MULTITENANT` are both unset — a non-loopback value implies `own_ops`. `WEBGATE_HOST` wins over `WEBVIEW_HOST` when both are set.", "advanced"),
    ("WEBVIEW_ALLOW_LOCAL_POSTURE", "WebView / Console (deployment posture, owner login, branding)", "OFF", "Escape hatch for the server-posture boot refusal: at `local` posture (loopback with owner login) the console refuses to start when the deployment looks like a server — `WEBVIEW_PUBLIC_URL` set, a `--proxy-headers`/`--forwarded-allow-ips` process argv, or a `POLYROB_DATA_DIR` out…", "advanced"),
    ("WEBVIEW_EMIT_URL", "WebView / Console (deployment posture, owner login, branding)", "unset", "Loopback-only authenticated fast-push, using a token derived from `API_AUTH_TOKEN` or `WEBGATE_JWT_SECRET`; unset credentials use the file watcher. Explicit override for the telemetry fast-push target (`/api/internal/emit`). Unset ⇒ `http://127.0.0.1:<WEBGATE_PORT or WEBVIEW_POR…", "advanced"),
    ("WEBGATE_JWT_SECRET", "WebView / Console (deployment posture, owner login, branding)", "unset (secret, masked)", "Fallback secret for the loopback telemetry fast-push token when `API_AUTH_TOKEN` is unset (HMAC-derived; the secret itself never travels). Both unset = no token, the file watcher carries the feed.", "advanced"),
    ("WEBGATE_PORT", "WebView / Console (deployment posture, owner login, branding)", "`5050`", "Bind port. `WEBGATE_PORT` wins over `WEBVIEW_PORT` when both are set. (`server_launcher.py`'s own code-level default is 3000; the production systemd unit sets `WEBVIEW_PORT=5050`, which `webgate.bind_port()` also defaults to.)", "advanced"),
    ("WEBVIEW_PORT", "WebView / Console (deployment posture, owner login, branding)", "`5050`", "Bind port. `WEBGATE_PORT` wins over `WEBVIEW_PORT` when both are set. (`server_launcher.py`'s own code-level default is 3000; the production systemd unit sets `WEBVIEW_PORT=5050`, which `webgate.bind_port()` also defaults to.)", "advanced"),
    ("POLYROB_OWNER_USERNAME", "WebView / Console (deployment posture, owner login, branding)", "unset", "Owner login username for `own_ops`/`multitenant` posture (Posture 1/2 console access). Both this and the hash below must be set for owner-login to be \"configured\"; if either is missing, login is refused.", "public"),
    ("POLYROB_OWNER_PASSWORD_HASH", "WebView / Console (deployment posture, owner login, branding)", "unset", "Argon2 hash of the owner password — never plaintext. `verify_owner_password` always runs a real argon2 verify (against a precomputed dummy hash when the username doesn't match) so a wrong username can't be distinguished from a wrong password by response timing. No CLI helper gen…", "public"),
    ("POLYROB_CONSOLE_NAME", "WebView / Console (deployment posture, owner login, branding)", "`\"POLYROB Console\"`", "Opt-in override of the web console's product display name. Unset keeps the framework brand even when `resolve_instance_id()` is a custom instance id — renaming the console is a deliberate, separate choice from naming the instance.", "advanced"),
    ("POLYROB_SUPPORT_URL", "WebView / Console (deployment posture, owner login, branding)", "`https://t.me/tmachinrobot`", "Support link shown in the console footer/help.", "advanced"),
    ("POLYROB_SUPPORT_HANDLE", "WebView / Console (deployment posture, owner login, branding)", "`@TMACHINROBOT`", "Support handle text shown alongside the support link.", "advanced"),
    ("POLYROB_BRAND_URL", "WebView / Console (deployment posture, owner login, branding)", "unset (`\"\"`)", "Instance brand URL; also the base for the derived `terms_url`/`privacy_url` defaults below. 043 A12: no placeholder-host default — an unset value renders no footer link at all, rather than a dead `your-polyrob-host.example` link.", "advanced"),
    ("POLYROB_ORG_URL", "WebView / Console (deployment posture, owner login, branding)", "unset (`\"\"`)", "Parent-org URL shown in the console footer. 043 A12: no default (was `https://theselfrule.org`, the framework author's own org, wrongly shown as \"your org\" on an unconfigured deploy); unset renders no footer link.", "advanced"),
    ("POLYROB_TERMS_URL", "WebView / Console (deployment posture, owner login, branding)", "`{POLYROB_BRAND_URL}/terms`, or unset (`\"\"`) if `POLYROB_BRAND_URL` is also unset", "Terms-of-service link. 043 A12: with no brand URL to derive from, this is empty and the footer renders no Terms link.", "advanced"),
    ("POLYROB_PRIVACY_URL", "WebView / Console (deployment posture, owner login, branding)", "`{POLYROB_BRAND_URL}/privacy`, or unset (`\"\"`) if `POLYROB_BRAND_URL` is also unset", "Privacy-policy link (same fix as above).", "advanced"),
    ("WEBVIEW_AUTH_ENABLED", "WebView / Console (deployment posture, owner login, branding)", "ON (`'true'`)", "Legacy compatibility flag. It cannot disable authentication in own_ops or multitenant postures. Local posture also requires owner login; loopback does not authenticate a caller.", "advanced"),
    ("WEBVIEW_FEED_DEFAULT_LIMIT", "WebView / Console (deployment posture, owner login, branding)", "`500`", "Default number of feed events returned by the console feed endpoints.", "advanced"),
    ("WEBVIEW_FEED_MAX_LIMIT", "WebView / Console (deployment posture, owner login, branding)", "`2000`", "Hard cap on a requested feed-event limit.", "advanced"),
    ("WEBVIEW_INSTALL_PREFIX", "WebView / Console (deployment posture, owner login, branding)", "`/opt/polyrob`", "Install prefix whose `logs/` dir the standalone webview launcher writes `webview.log` into.", "advanced"),
    ("WEBVIEW_LOG_LEVEL", "WebView / Console (deployment posture, owner login, branding)", "`info`", "Default `--log-level` for the standalone webview launcher.", "advanced"),
    ("WEBVIEW_VERSION", "WebView / Console (deployment posture, owner login, branding)", "unset (= the installed package version)", "Explicit override of the version string the console displays (for deployments that pin it).", "advanced"),
    ("WEBVIEW_WS_URL", "WebView / Console (deployment posture, owner login, branding)", "unset (`''` = same-origin)", "Explicit Socket.IO endpoint URL handed to the console frontend; unset connects same-origin.", "advanced"),
    ("DATA_PERMS_MAX_ENTRIES", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`200000`", "057 WS-G: entry budget for the data-home permission walk (`polyrob doctor --perms`, the status `security` line); over it the report says `truncated` and names the budget — \"no offenders in the first N\" is not \"no offenders\".", "advanced"),
    ("POLYROB_ALLOW_ROOT_CLI", "Misc / runtime knobs", "OFF (`false`)", "057 WS-G: let a root-run owner CLI verb WRITE the deployed data home (script escape hatch; `--as-root` is the interactive one). Otherwise a root euid on a deployed box refuses write verbs with the remedy `sudo -u polyrob-agent polyrob …` — a root-owned row is what locked the ser…", "advanced"),
    ("TWITTER_ENABLED", "Misc / runtime knobs", "OFF (`'false'`) (ON under `AUTONOMY_MODE=autonomous`)", "Enable the Twitter/X write surface.", "public"),
    ("TWITTER_REQUIRE_APPROVAL", "Misc / runtime knobs", "ON (`'true'`)", "Ask the owner once more before an X write on a genuine owner turn (OFF = the owner's request is the approval). Autonomous, forged, room and read-tainted turns always need a real owner approval, whatever this says.", "advanced"),
    ("TWITTER_POST_COOLDOWN_ENABLED", "Misc / runtime knobs", "**ON**", "2026-08-28: durable, cross-session minimum gap between AUTONOMOUS `twitter_post`/`twitter_thread` writes (a repeat goal re-firing in a fresh session, each with its own fresh in-memory rate-limit bucket, posted 30+ near-duplicate tweets over ~5 days — the in-memory `TWITTER_WRITE…", "advanced"),
    ("TWITTER_POST_COOLDOWN_SEC", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`3600`", "Minimum seconds between two autonomous `twitter_post`/`twitter_thread` writes for the same tenant, enforced by `TWITTER_POST_COOLDOWN_ENABLED`.", "advanced"),
    ("X_BROWSER_ENABLED", "Misc / runtime knobs", "OFF", "Register the captured-session `x_browser` tool for visible-inbox reads, existing-thread DM sends, posting, and self-registration. OFF by default; high_impact + delegate_blocked. `x_post`/`x_dm` are owner-approval-gated and `x_signup_start` is always owner-queued. Needs `polyrob…", "advanced"),
    ("X_SIGNUP_HANDLE", "Misc / runtime knobs", "unset (= the instance id)", "The @handle `x_signup_start` REQUESTS for the agent's own X account (sanitised to letters/digits/underscore, ≤15 chars). An instance id is often already taken on X, so this lets an operator pick another. The live handle X actually assigned is reported back — a refused request ke…", "advanced"),
    ("X_SIGNUP_DISCLOSURE", "Misc / runtime knobs", "unset (= `Automated account: <instance> is an autonomous POLYROB agent. Posts are generated by software.`)", "The automation-disclosure bio the signup writes to the new X profile (≤160 chars). The default names the INSTANCE, never the owner's internal tenant id (the old text rendered `operated by local`). Whether it was actually applied is reported (`bio_applied`), never assumed.", "advanced"),
    ("ALLOWED_REASONING_TURNS", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`1`", "Tool-free planning turns allowed before escalation.", "advanced"),
    ("COMPACTION_COOLDOWN_STEPS", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`8`", "Minimum steps between LLM-compaction firings in the 85–95 % band. Raised 3 → 8 on 2026-09-23 (063 F11): at 3 the band could fire again almost immediately and each rebuild colds the whole conversation prefix. The cooldown is a FLOOR, not a wall — a compaction that actually cut ≥…", "advanced"),
    ("COMPACTION_WARM_PREFIX", "Misc / runtime knobs", "**ON**", "063 F11 (2026-09-23): when no distinct aux model is configured (`compaction_llm is self.llm`), the compaction summariser sends `[foundation + the messages being summarised + ONE trailing instruction]` instead of a lone `HumanMessage` carrying the conversation as TEXT. The leadin…", "internal"),
    ("COMPACTION_PROMPT_GUARD", "Misc / runtime knobs", "**ON**", "Anti-injection framing on the compaction summarizer prompt + rebuilt summary.", "advanced"),
    ("COMPACTION_KEEP_RECENT", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`10`", "Min recent messages kept verbatim.", "advanced"),
    ("COMPACTION_TAIL_TOKEN_RATIO", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`0.20`", "Tail kept by token budget.", "advanced"),
    ("COMPACTION_PER_MSG_CHARS", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`3000`", "Per-message head+tail budget into summarizer.", "advanced"),
    ("COMPACTION_TOOL_RESULT_CHARS", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`2000`", "Tool-result budget into summarizer.", "advanced"),
    ("COMPACTION_MAX_SUMMARY_TOKENS", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`12000`", "Summary budget ceiling.", "advanced"),
    ("COMPACTION_MIN_SUMMARY_TOKENS", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`2000`", "Summary budget floor.", "advanced"),
    ("COMPACTION_MIN_SAVINGS_PCT", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`10.0`", "Anti-thrash back-off threshold.", "advanced"),
    ("COMPACTION_CHECKPOINT", "Misc / runtime knobs", "ON (`'true'`)", "Dump pre-compaction trajectory.", "advanced"),
    ("CONTEXT_OVERFLOW_THRESHOLD", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`0.90`", "Context-usage fraction triggering overflow handling.", "advanced"),
    ("MAX_REPETITIONS", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`2` (dev) / `3` (prod)", "Loop-detection repeat threshold.", "advanced"),
    ("UNCHANGED_STATE_THRESHOLD", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`3` (dev) / `4` (prod)", "Unchanged-state loop threshold.", "advanced"),
    ("EMPTY_ACTION_FAST_ESCALATE", "Misc / runtime knobs", "ON (`'true'`)", "Escalate fast on empty-action loops.", "advanced"),
    ("MIN_STEPS_BEFORE_DONE", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`3`", "Minimum steps before `done()` is honored.", "advanced"),
    ("STEP_TIMEOUT_SECONDS", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`300`", "Per-step timeout.", "advanced"),
    ("STALL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`300`", "Stall detection.", "advanced"),
    ("LLM_BASE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`30`", "Base LLM timeout (adjusted up by token count).", "advanced"),
    ("LLM_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_SECONDS", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`120`", "Standard LLM request timeout.", "advanced"),
    ("LLM_STREAM_TIMEOUT_SECONDS", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`300`", "Streaming LLM timeout.", "advanced"),
    ("MCP_TIMEOUT_SECONDS", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`180`", "Per-action timeout the Controller applies to an `mcp` tool call (network / subprocess latency).", "advanced"),
    ("BROWSER_TIMEOUT_SECONDS", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`120`", "Per-action timeout for a `browser` tool call (page loads, DOM operations).", "advanced"),
    ("FILESYSTEM_TIMEOUT_SECONDS", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`30`", "Per-action timeout for a `filesystem` tool call.", "advanced"),
    ("POLYMARKET_TIMEOUT_SECONDS", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`60`", "Per-action timeout for a `polymarket` tool call.", "advanced"),
    ("SHELL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`630`", "Per-action timeout for a `shell` tool call. Sits ABOVE `SHELL_MAX_TIMEOUT_SEC` (600) so the tool's own clean kill, with its output, wins.", "advanced"),
    ("CODE_EXEC_TIMEOUT_SECONDS", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`630`", "Per-action timeout for a `code_execution` AND a `coding` tool call (`coding.run_tests` runs on the same backend with the same ceiling; under the 60 s default it was killed first); above the tool's own ceiling for the same reason as `SHELL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS`.", "advanced"),
    ("DEFAULT_TOOL_TIMEOUT_SECONDS", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`180`", "Per-action timeout for every tool without its own entry. `defi_data`'s pricing budget (`DEFI_PORTFOLIO_PRICE_BUDGET_SEC`) must stay below it.", "advanced"),
    ("MAX_PARSE_RETRIES", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`3`", "JSON-from-text parse retries (fallback path).", "advanced"),
    ("ENABLE_ROBUST_PARSE", "Misc / runtime knobs", "ON", "Master switch for the robust JSON-from-text parse machinery (retries + template hints on the non-native-tools path).", "advanced"),
    ("ENABLE_JSON_TEMPLATE_RETRY", "Misc / runtime knobs", "ON", "On a parse failure, retry with an explicit JSON-template hint (bounded by `MAX_PARSE_RETRIES`).", "advanced"),
    ("BASE_RETRY_DELAY", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`1`", "Base delay (seconds) for the parse-retry exponential backoff.", "advanced"),
    ("MAX_RETRY_DELAY", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`5`", "Cap (seconds) on the parse-retry backoff delay.", "advanced"),
    ("BACKOFF_MULTIPLIER", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`1.5`", "Multiplier for the parse-retry exponential backoff.", "advanced"),
    ("ENABLE_CONTEXT_OVERFLOW_GUARD", "Misc / runtime knobs", "ON", "Abort a step whose estimated tokens exceed `CONTEXT_OVERFLOW_THRESHOLD` of the model's context window.", "advanced"),
    ("SAFETY_MARGIN_PERCENT", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`0.05`", "Fraction of the input-token budget held back as safety margin by the token counter.", "advanced"),
    ("REQUIRE_SCHEMA_KEYS", "Misc / runtime knobs", "OFF", "Strict JSON-candidate validation: require `current_state`+`action` keys before accepting a parsed candidate.", "advanced"),
    ("INJECT_FORMAT_HINT_EARLY", "Misc / runtime knobs", "ON", "Inject the JSON format hint proactively on the non-native-tools path (instead of only after a failure).", "advanced"),
    ("FORCE_RECALIBRATE_AFTER_LARGE_ACTIONS", "Misc / runtime knobs", "ON", "Force a token-count recalibration after an action result over `LARGE_ACTION_THRESHOLD` chars.", "advanced"),
    ("LARGE_ACTION_THRESHOLD", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`500`", "Result size (chars) that counts as a \"large action\" for recalibration.", "advanced"),
    ("STRIP_BASE64_IMAGES", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`true`", "Strip `data:image/...;base64,` blobs from parsed page content (`false` disables).", "advanced"),
    ("TOOL_RESULT_AGE_CHARS", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`2000`", "063 F15 (2026-09-23): at a compaction boundary — and ONLY there, which is already a cold prefix — every `ToolMessage` outside the protected tail (the newest 6) longer than this is demoted to its first line plus a NAMED pointer: the `read_file(file_path=…)` line the offload path…", "advanced"),
    ("MEDIA_KEEP_MAX", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`6`", "F7: image-bearing turns the conversation may hold before ANY is retired. Below it nothing is rewritten, so consecutive requests share a prompt prefix. The old rule anchored on the newest image and re-wrote the previously-newest turn every step.", "advanced"),
    ("MEDIA_RETIRE_BATCH", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`4`", "F7: image turns whose base64 is retired in ONE step once `MEDIA_KEEP_MAX` is passed (the pass always retires at least enough to land back at the ceiling, so a second pass is a no-op).", "advanced"),
    ("MEDIA_KEEP_FLOOR", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`2`", "F7: newest image turns never retired, whatever the count — vision continuity for the current turn.", "advanced"),
    ("STATE_MESSAGE_EPHEMERAL", "Misc / runtime knobs", "**ON**", "F16(ii) (2026-09-23): the per-step state message (step counter, clock, brain-state continuity, browser DOM + screenshot) rides the ONE-SHOT ephemeral rail instead of being appended into `history` and spliced back out mid-deque after the call. The splice rebuilt the whole deque e…", "internal"),
    ("MAX_USER_GUIDANCE_TOKENS", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`3000`", "Token budget for injected user-guidance messages (head+tail middle-elision past it). A second reader in `agent/core/resources.py` uses its own default `1000` for the resource-manager cap.", "advanced"),
    ("MAX_USER_MESSAGES_PER_STEP", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`3`", "Max queued user messages drained into one step.", "advanced"),
    ("USER_MESSAGE_TRUNCATE_LENGTH", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`4000`", "Per-message char budget for a genuine user message (head+tail elision, never a blunt cut).", "advanced"),
    ("USER_MESSAGE_KEEP_TAIL", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`500`", "Tail chars kept by the user-message elision.", "advanced"),
    ("FORGED_MESSAGE_MAX_CHARS", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`16000`", "Ceiling for a forged (self-wake / delegation-result, pre-wrapped) message body — large enough that a bounded payload passes untouched with its closing delimiter intact.", "advanced"),
    ("FORGED_MESSAGE_KEEP_TAIL", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`3000`", "Tail chars kept when a forged message does exceed its ceiling.", "advanced"),
    ("MAX_EXTRACTED_CONTENT_SIZE", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`100000`", "Threshold (chars) above which ONE tool result is offloaded to a workspace file with a preview (the LIVE offload path). F26: lowered from 500000 (~125K tokens, a threshold the disk-pointer path almost never reached) to a reference agent's per-result number, ~25K tokens. `0` = off.", "advanced"),
    ("MAX_EXTRACTED_CONTENT_TURN_SIZE", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`200000`", "Threshold (chars) on the SUM of a turn's tool results. Three 80K-char results each pass the per-result test above and together are 240K chars of context; over this the LARGEST results go to disk first until the turn fits. `0` = off.", "advanced"),
    ("LARGE_CONTENT_PREVIEW_LENGTH", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`15000`", "Preview chars kept in-context when a result is offloaded to a file.", "advanced"),
    ("STORE_LARGE_CONTENT_AS_FILES", "Misc / runtime knobs", "ON / `500000`", "Consulted only by the legacy `should_store_content_as_file` helper (test-pinned; no production caller today — the live offload path keys on `MAX_EXTRACTED_CONTENT_SIZE` above).", "advanced"),
    ("MAX_EXTRACTED_CONTENT_LENGTH", "Misc / runtime knobs", "ON / `500000`", "Consulted only by the legacy `should_store_content_as_file` helper (test-pinned; no production caller today — the live offload path keys on `MAX_EXTRACTED_CONTENT_SIZE` above).", "advanced"),
    ("MAX_ERROR_LENGTH", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`2000`", "Char cap on a tool ERROR result echoed into history (tail-kept).", "advanced"),
    ("MAX_SUCCESS_LENGTH", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`100000`", "Char cap on a tool SUCCESS result echoed into history.", "advanced"),
    ("TASK_MODE", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`BALANCED`", "Task agent mode preset.", "advanced"),
    ("TASK_PERSONALITY_BLOCK", "Misc / runtime knobs", "ON under `POLYROB_LOCAL`, OFF on the server", "Inject the `<identity>` persona block into the task agent. The live seam is an ACCESS-TIME function returning `local_mode_enabled()` — not the literal `'false'` this row used to claim, which made `config get`/`config list` state the opposite of the runtime for every local CLI us…", "internal"),
    ("ANONYMIZED_TELEMETRY", "Misc / runtime knobs", "OFF (`false`)", "Opt-in anonymized PostHog product analytics (027 WP5: never on by default). Only an explicit `true` enables it.", "advanced"),
    ("VALIDATE_OUTPUT", "Misc / runtime knobs", "OFF", "Judge-backed validation of the agent's final answer before it's accepted (wired through the lazily provisioned auxiliary judge model and fail-open to the main model). An explicit `AgentConfig(validate_output=...)` kwarg still wins over this env default.", "advanced"),
    ("INTERRUPT_REDIRECT", "Misc / runtime knobs", "OFF", "Ctrl-C mid-turn prompts for a redirect instruction that becomes the next turn instead of silently aborting. Deliberately not in `_SAFE_LOCAL_FLAGS` — it changes SIGINT UX for all local users, so it stays an explicit opt-in even under `POLYROB_LOCAL`.", "advanced"),
    ("POLYROB_ENV", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`development` (falls back to `ENVIRONMENT`)", "Deployment environment name; `production`/`prod` makes the MCP encryption layer require a real `MCP_ENCRYPTION_KEY` instead of the dev key file.", "advanced"),
    ("POLYROB_ENV_KEY_BACKFILL", "Misc / runtime knobs", "OFF", "DEPRECATED (deleted next release): legacy local-mode backfill of secret keys from `config/.env.*` into the process env. Set truthy for one more release of the legacy behavior; the replacement is the explicit `polyrob config migrate` verb. When unset and the old path would have f…", "internal"),
    ("POLYROB_HOME", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`~/.polyrob`", "Override for the polyrob home directory (CLI config, keys, home-migration target). In profile mode `apply_profile_env` points it at the profile's home.", "public"),
    ("POLYROB_PROFILE", "Misc / runtime knobs", "unset", "Named-profile selection (tier 2; the `-P`/`--profile` flag is tier 1 and overwrites it). A profile is an isolated home under `<base>/profiles/<name>/`; selecting one sets `POLYROB_HOME`/`POLYROB_DATA_DIR` to it. Present-but-EMPTY = explicit \"no profile\" (disables the project-pin…", "public"),
    ("POLYROB_PROFILE_SOURCE", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`env`", "Internal hand-off, set by `activate_profile` for child processes: records WHICH tier (flag/pin/sticky/env) selected the active profile so children report the original source. Not an operator knob.", "advanced"),
    ("POLYROB_PROFILES_ROOT", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`polyrob_home()/profiles`", "Location of the profile registry + parent of the sticky file. Pinned automatically by `apply_profile_env` BEFORE `POLYROB_HOME` moves inside a profile, so in-profile `polyrob profile …` commands still see the shared registry. Override for tests/relocation.", "advanced"),
    ("POLYROB_ALLOW_CROSS_PROFILE", "Misc / runtime knobs", "OFF", "Opt-in bypass of the cross-profile file guard: with it OFF, the filesystem/coding tools refuse to touch ANOTHER profile's home (defense-in-depth, not a security boundary).", "advanced"),
    ("POLYROB_BIN_DIR", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`~/.local/bin`", "Where `polyrob profile create/alias` writes per-profile wrapper commands (`<name>` → `polyrob -P <name>`).", "advanced"),
    ("PERSONALITY_DEFAULT_CHARACTER", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`polyrob`", "Which `<name>.character.json` renders the default persona. The package ships the neutral `polyrob` character plus six curated personas (`default`, `writer`, `researcher`, `analyst`, `coder`, `ops` in `data/characters/`); a specific bot's own character is data in `<data_dir>/char…", "advanced"),
    ("POLYROB_IN_DOCKER", "Misc / runtime knobs", "unset", "Force the self-update detector to classify the install as Docker (normally auto-detected via `/.dockerenv`); updates then mean \"rebuild the image\".", "advanced"),
    ("POLYROB_NONINTERACTIVE", "Misc / runtime knobs", "unset", "Truthy ⇒ never prompt interactively (suppresses the inline API-key wizard; same effect as `CI=true`).", "advanced"),
    ("POLYROB_PERSISTENT_INPUT", "Misc / runtime knobs", "ON", "REPL uses the long-lived bottom-anchored prompt_toolkit input; set `0`/`off` for the legacy ephemeral prompt. Retire after 1.4.", "internal"),
    ("POLYROB_PERSONA", "Misc / runtime knobs", "unset", "Persona for the CLI agent's `<identity>`: a known template key renders that template's persona (and seeds its skills); any other non-empty value is used as literal free-form persona text. Only applied when the personality block is enabled.", "advanced"),
    ("POLYROB_PLAIN", "Misc / runtime knobs", "OFF", "Force the plain (non-Rich) CLI renderer; mirrors `--plain` (the flag wins). Render toggle only — does not imply non-interactive.", "advanced"),
    ("POLYROB_WORKSPACE_LOCK_DIR", "Misc / runtime knobs", "set by bootstrap", "Directory for the CLI workspace lock (interactive-gate/CWD-corruption guard). Set automatically by `build_cli_container`; override only for tests/multi-instance layouts.", "advanced"),
    ("TASK_MAX_MESSAGES", "Misc / runtime knobs", "unset (= model-derived)", "Explicit override of MessageManager's max-message window; non-numeric values are ignored with a WARN.", "advanced"),
    ("CONFIDENCE_CHECK_BEFORE_DONE", "Misc / runtime knobs", "ON", "BALANCED-mode preset: run the confidence check before honoring `done()`.", "advanced"),
    ("TASK_VERIFICATION_REQUIRED", "Misc / runtime knobs", "ON", "BALANCED-mode preset: require task verification before completion.", "advanced"),
    ("HISTORY_SECRET_SCRUB", "Misc / runtime knobs", "ON", "Pattern-based secret scrub (conservative shapes only) over message history, even with no sensitive-data allowlist registered; `off` restores allowlist-only.", "advanced"),
    ("SOURCE_PRECEDENCE_PROMPT", "Misc / runtime knobs", "ON", "Separate instruction authority from factual freshness: system/runtime policy applies; the latest genuine owner/user instruction can revise the pinned task; tool results and memory remain data.", "advanced"),
    ("AUTO_AGENT_INIT", "Misc / runtime knobs", "OFF", "Run the task-agent module initializer at import instead of lazily.", "advanced"),
    ("PROFILE_MEM", "Misc / runtime knobs", "unset (`1` enables)", "Dev: register an atexit memory-profile dump for the agent process (tracemalloc-based).", "advanced"),
    ("BROWSER_USE_LOGGING_LEVEL", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`info`", "`debug` turns on verbose telemetry-service debug logging.", "internal"),
    ("POSTHOG_API_KEY", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`phx_dev_fallback_key` (secret, masked)", "PostHog project key for anonymized telemetry (rides `ANONYMIZED_TELEMETRY`); the checked-in default is a non-functional dev placeholder.", "advanced"),
    ("TELEMETRY_BUFFER_SIZE", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`500`", "Telemetry event-buffer size per session before a flush.", "advanced"),
    ("TELEMETRY_BUFFER_TIMEOUT", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`60.0`", "Seconds before a partial telemetry buffer is flushed.", "advanced"),
    ("TELEMETRY_EVENTS_MAX_BYTES", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`10485760` (10 MB)", "Rotate a session's `events.jsonl` past this size.", "advanced"),
    ("TELEMETRY_FEED_MAX_FILES", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`200`", "Max feed files kept per session by feed retention.", "advanced"),
    ("TELEMETRY_FEED_MAX_AGE_HOURS", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`168` (7 days)", "Max age of kept feed files.", "advanced"),
    ("TELEMETRY_FEED_RETENTION_EVERY", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`50`", "Run feed retention every N feed writes (min 1).", "advanced"),
    ("LAZY_DEPS_MODE", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`trusted`", "066 P1: how `core.lazy_deps.ensure` installs an ALLOWLISTED optional extra on first use (a Gemini turn installs the Gemini SDK; a PDF read installs `[docs]`). `trusted` = the feature's shipped, HASHED closure (`core/lazy_closures/<feature>.txt`, generated from `requirements.lock…", "advanced"),
    ("LAZY_DEPS_ENABLED", "Misc / runtime knobs", "unset", "Deprecated by `LAZY_DEPS_MODE` (which wins when set): `true` = `trusted`, `false` = `off`. Retire after 1.4.", "internal"),
    ("POLYROB_PACKS", "Misc / runtime knobs", "unset", "067 P2: comma list of the pack ids that load (the `polyrob.packs` entry points). Unset or blank = every installed FIRST-PARTY pack; a third-party pack loads only when named here, and never while wallet custody or remote signing is enabled. Read when a process loads its packs; a…", "advanced"),
    ("POLYROB_PACKS_DISABLED", "Misc / runtime knobs", "unset", "067 P2: comma list of pack ids that never load, even when named in `POLYROB_PACKS` (disabled wins). Their policy rows still register (data only); their code, tools, skills, CLI commands and routers do not. `polyrob pack disable <id>` writes it.", "advanced"),
    ("POLYROB_BOOTSTRAP_STAGES", "Misc / runtime knobs", "unset", "Set by `install.sh`, not by you. A JSON object (`install_method`, `source_dir`, `venv_dir`, `command`, `stages[]`) that the installer hands to `polyrob setup` so ONE writer records the install in `<config home>/.polyrob-bootstrap.json`. Only those keys are kept, and a malformed…", "advanced"),
    ("TOOL_USAGE_TELEMETRY", "Misc / runtime knobs", "ON", "Emit one `tool_invoked` event (`{tool, action, ok, ms}`) per tool action the controller runs, success or error, into the durable event log — the only cross-session \"is this tool used?\" signal, rendered by the status snapshot's `tools` section. OFF is byte-identical to before the…", "internal"),
    ("TELEMETRY_EVENT_LOG_ENABLED", "Misc / runtime knobs", "ON", "The durable telemetry event log (`telemetry_events.db`) — additive observability sink, fail-open; `off` disables.", "advanced"),
    ("TELEMETRY_EVENT_LOG_RETENTION_DAYS", "Misc / runtime knobs", "`30` (min 1)", "Prune event-log rows older than this on the heartbeat ticker.", "advanced"),
    ("EXTERNAL_WRITE_TELEMETRY", "Misc / runtime knobs", "ON", "033: record one `external_write` row per outward act — classified `social`/`comms`/`public`/`money`/`code`/`self`/`network` by `core/effects.py` at the Controller post-hook, the two `MessageRouter` sends and the no-Controller writers (cron delivery, app supervisor, settlement no…", "advanced"),
    ("EXTERNAL_WRITE_PAUSE_GATE", "Misc / runtime knobs", "ON", "033: the Controller effect pre-hook refuses an AUTONOMOUS or forged `social`/`comms`/`public`/`money` write while the matching 031 pause covers it (`social_post`, `outbound_comms`, `oversight_deploy` / `app_deploy`, `spend`), and records the refusal as `outcome=denied`. An owner…", "advanced"),
    ("EXTERNAL_WRITE_STRICT", "Misc / runtime knobs", "OFF", "033: refuse a write verb that has no explicit row in `core/effects.py` (`WRITE_ACTIONS`/`NON_WRITE_ACTIONS`) instead of recording it at the tool's ceiling with `confidence=tool`. MCP actions are exempt (a third-party server names them at runtime).", "advanced"),
    ("SECURITY_EVENT_LOG_ENABLED", "Misc / runtime knobs", "ON", "045 lanes 1-3: record every inbound routing decision, every gate refusal and every threat-scan flag into the durable event log. Bodies are never stored (length + an 8-char hash only). OFF is byte-identical to pre-045. Retention rides `TELEMETRY_EVENT_LOG_RETENTION_DAYS`. Retire…", "internal"),
    ("TWITTER_API_KEY", "Misc / runtime knobs", "unset (secret, masked)", "OAuth 1.0a user-context credentials for the twitter tool, the X DM surface, and `polyrob avatar push --twitter`; explicit creds passed to the client win over env.", "public"),
    ("TWITTER_API_SECRET_KEY", "Misc / runtime knobs", "unset (secret, masked)", "OAuth 1.0a user-context credentials for the twitter tool, the X DM surface, and `polyrob avatar push --twitter`; explicit creds passed to the client win over env.", "advanced"),
    ("TWITTER_ACCESS_TOKEN", "Misc / runtime knobs", "unset (secret, masked)", "OAuth 1.0a user-context credentials for the twitter tool, the X DM surface, and `polyrob avatar push --twitter`; explicit creds passed to the client win over env.", "advanced"),
    ("TWITTER_ACCESS_TOKEN_SECRET", "Misc / runtime knobs", "unset (secret, masked)", "OAuth 1.0a user-context credentials for the twitter tool, the X DM surface, and `polyrob avatar push --twitter`; explicit creds passed to the client win over env.", "advanced"),
    ("TWITTER_OAUTH2_ACCESS_TOKEN", "Misc / runtime knobs", "unset (secret, masked)", "OAuth 2.0 PKCE user access token with `dm.read`, `users.read`, and `tweet.read` (plus `dm.write` when sending). Enables the encrypted X Chat API; the app-only `TWITTER_BEARER_TOKEN` cannot read private messages. Since 2026-09-17 every consumer reads it through `packs/x/polyrob_x…", "advanced"),
    ("TWITTER_OAUTH2_REFRESH_TOKEN", "Misc / runtime knobs", "unset (secret, masked)", "The OAuth 2.0 refresh token that pairs with `TWITTER_OAUTH2_ACCESS_TOKEN` (issued only when the grant asked for `offline.access`). When BOTH are set, the pair is seeded ONCE into the encrypted X token store (`<data_home>/.x_session.json`, provider `x_oauth2`) on first use and re…", "advanced"),
    ("TWITTER_OAUTH2_CLIENT_ID", "Misc / runtime knobs", "unset", "The X app's OAuth 2.0 Client ID (developer.x.com → app → Keys and tokens). Required to REFRESH a user token or to run `polyrob x-account oauth-login` (PKCE). Not a secret, but the refresh endpoint refuses without it — a stored pair can be USED but not RENEWED while this is unset.", "advanced"),
    ("TWITTER_OAUTH2_CLIENT_SECRET", "Misc / runtime knobs", "unset (secret, masked)", "The app's OAuth 2.0 Client Secret, needed only for a *confidential* app (X then wants HTTP Basic on the token endpoint). Leave unset for a public (PKCE-only) app.", "advanced"),
    ("X_OAUTH2_REDIRECT_URI", "Misc / runtime knobs", "unset", "The console URL X redirects the owner's browser to after `/x login` — exactly `https://<console host>/api/packs/x/oauth/callback` (http only for 127.0.0.1/localhost), and registered as a callback URI of the X app (developer.x.com → app → User authentication settings). Set it in…", "advanced"),
    ("TWITTER_CHAT_PASSPHRASE", "Misc / runtime knobs", "unset (secret, masked)", "X Chat secure-key-backup passphrase/PIN. When set with the OAuth2 user token, the official Chat XDK unlocks the account keys and decrypts API event ciphertext. Treat this as a root credential.", "advanced"),
